yle="background:#fff3e0;color:#e65100" data-s="Macarius/Symeon" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'Macarius/Symeon');">Macarius/Symeon</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#fff3e0;color:#e65100" data-s="Epiphanius" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'Epiphanius');">Epiphanius</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#fff3e0;color:#e65100" title=": &ldquo;(Hom. v. [iv.] in Joan. c. 1, 2) Or to give an other explanation. We will not put the stop at without Him was not any thing made, as the heretics do. ...&rdquo;" data-s="Chrysostom" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'Chrysostom');">Chrysostom</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#fff3e0;color:#e65100" title=": &ldquo;CHAPTER VI. That the Son is by Nature Life and therefore not originate, but of the Essence of God the Father.  That which was made, in it was Life.  Y...&rdquo;" data-s="Cyril" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'Cyril');">Cyril</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#fff3e0;color:#e65100" data-s="Hesychius" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'Hesychius');">Hesychius</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#fff3e0;color:#e65100" data-s="Theodoret" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'Theodoret');">Theodoret</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#fff3e0;color:#e65100" data-s="Victorinus-Rome1/5" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'Victorinus-Rome1/5');">Victorinus-Rome1/5</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#fff3e0;color:#e65100" title=": &ldquo;Many read this inaccurately because they add without any punctuation, “that which has been made in him was life.” The correct statement is “All things...&rdquo;" data-s="Jerome" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'Jerome');">Jerome</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#fff3e0;color:#e65100" title="Sermon XCI.: &ldquo;196 Rom. i. 22. 4197 Rom. i. 23. 4198 Totum. 4199 John i. 4.   the Truth, 