v class="tc-criterion-exp">La lectura ἦν tiene el apoyo de la gran mayoría de manuscritos importantes y diversas tradiciones textuales. Esta amplia atestación sugiere que es la lectura original.</div></div><div class="tc-criterion-item"><strong>Estructura retórica</strong><div class="tc-criterion-exp">El imperfecto ἦν mantiene la consistencia con el patrón de imperfectos en los versículos precedentes del prólogo. El cambio a presente rompería esta estructura retórica establecida.</div></div></div><div style="font-size:0.72rem;color:#1565c0;margin-top:0.5rem;cursor:pointer" onclick="document.getElementById('exeg-4')?.classList.remove('collapsed');document.getElementById('exeg-4')?.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'})">↑ Ver análisis exegético de este versículo</div><div style="margin-top:0.8rem;text-align:center"><a href="tc_deep_dive_John_1_4.html" onclick="if(!this.dataset.ready){this.textContent='⏳ Generando análisis profundo...';this.style.opacity=0.6;return true;}" style="display:inline-block;padding:8px 20px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a237e,#0d47a1);color:white;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.85rem;font-weight:600;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(26,35,126,0.3)">🔍 Deep Dive — Análisis completo de esta variante</a><div style="font-size:0.7rem;color:#888;margin-top:3px">Si la página no existe, usa el tool <code>critical_apparatus</code> → <code>tc_deep_dive</code> en el MCP server para generarla.</div></div></div></div><div class="verse-block" id="vb5"><div class="verse-header"><span class="vnum">5</span></div><div class="greek-line" id="greek-5">καὶ τὸ φῶς ἐν τῇ σκοτίᾳ φαίνει καὶ ἡ σκοτία αὐτὸ οὐ κατέλαβεν</div><div class="uncial-line" id="uncial-5" style="display:none;font-family:'Noto Serif',serif;font-size:0.9rem;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#5d4037;background:#efebe9;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;overflow-wrap:break-word" title="Así se vería este versículo en un manuscrito uncial del siglo IV — todo mayúsculas, sin espacios (puntos medios añadidos como ayuda visual)">ΚΑΙ·ΤΟ·ΦΩΣ·ΕΝ·ΤΗΙ·ΣΚΟΤΙΑΙ·ΦΑΙΝΕΙ·ΚΑΙ·Η·ΣΚΟΤΙΑ·ΑΥΤΟ·ΟΥ·ΚΑΤΕΛΑΒΕΝ<span style="display:block;font-size:0.65rem;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:0;opacity:0.7"><a href="https://www.codexsinaiticus.org/en/manuscript.aspx?book=33&chapter=1&verse=5" target="_blank" style="color:#5d4037">Ver en Codex Sinaiticus →</a></span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:0.3rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:0.3rem;align-items:center"><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="toggleRVR(5)">RVR60</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('uncial-5').style.display=document.getElementById('uncial-5').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#efebe9;color:#5d4037;border-color:#bcaaa4" title="Escritura uncial: así se veía el NT en los manuscritos del s.IV (Vaticanus, Sinaiticus). Todo mayúsculas, sin espacios entre palabras (scriptio continua), sin acentos ni puntuación. La iota subscrita se escribe explícitamente.">Uncial</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('pron-5').style.display=document.getElementById('pron-5').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0;border-color:#90caf9" title="Pronunciación bizantina aproximada (griego moderno/eclesiástico)">Pronunciación</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-patr" onclick="toggleSection('patr-5')" title="28 citas patrísticas disponibles">✝ 28 patrística</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-exeg" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-5')" title="3 comentarios exegéticos">📚 3 exégesis</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-ver" onclick="document.getElementById('vers-5').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="9 versiones disponibles">📖 versiones</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('xrefs-5').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="8 referencias cruzadas">🔗 8 refs</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="copyVerse(5)" title="Copiar versículo al portapapeles" style="background:#f3e5f5;border-color:#ce93d8;color:#6a1b9a">📋</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('notes-5').style.display=document.getElementById('notes-5').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" title="Notas personales" style="background:#fff8e1;border-color:#ffd54f;color:#f57f17">📝</div></div><div id="rvr-5" class="collapsed spanish-line">La luz en las tinieblas resplandece, y las tinieblas no prevalecieron contra ella.</div><div id="vers-5" class="collapsed" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR60</span>La luz en las tinieblas resplandece, y las tinieblas no prevalecieron contra ella.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR1909</span>Y la luz en las tinieblas resplandece; mas las tinieblas no la comprendieron.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">KJV</span>And the light shineth in darkness; and the darkness comprehended it not.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">ASV</span>And the light shineth in the darkness; and the darkness apprehended it not. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">BSB</span>The Light shines in the darkness, and the darkness has not overcome it. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Darby</span>And the light appears in darkness, and the darkness apprehended it not. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">LITV</span>and the light shines in the darkness, and the darkness did not overtake it. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">YLT</span>and the light in the darkness did shine, and the darkness did not perceive it.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Vulgate</span>et lux in tenebris lucet et tenebrae eam non conprehenderunt</div></div><div id="xrefs-5" class="collapsed xref-container" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 Corinthians 2:14" data-es="Mas el hombre animal no percibe las cosas que son del Espíritu de Dios, porque le son locura: y no las puede entender, porque se han de examinar espiritualmente." data-gr="Ψυχικὸς δὲ ἄνθρωπος οὐ δέχεται τὰ τοῦ πνεύματος τοῦ θεοῦ, μωρία γὰρ αὐτῷ ἐστίν, καὶ οὐ δύναται γνῶναι, ὅτι πνευματικῶς ἀνακρίνεται·" data-lxx="" title="Mas el hombre animal no percibe las cosas que son del Espíritu de Dios, porque l…">1 Corinthians 2:14</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Job 24:13" data-es="Ellos son los que, rebeldes á la luz, Nunca conocieron sus caminos, Ni estuvieron en sus veredas." data-gr="הֵ֤מָּה הָיוּ֮ בְּֽ/מֹרְדֵ֫י א֥וֹר לֹֽא הִכִּ֥ירוּ דְרָכָ֑י/ו וְ/לֹ֥א יָ֝שְׁב֗וּ בִּ/נְתִיבֹתָֽי/ו" data-lxx="ἐπὶ γῆς ὄντων αὐτῶν καὶ οὐκ ἐπέγνωσαν ὁδὸν δὲ δικαιοσύνης οὐκ ᾔδεισαν οὐδὲ ἀτραποὺς αὐτῆς ἐπορεύθησαν" title="Ellos son los que, rebeldes á la luz, Nunca conocieron sus caminos, Ni estuviero…">Job 24:13</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Job 24:17" data-es="Porque la mañana es á todos ellos como sombra de muerte; Si son conocidos, terrores de sombra de muerte los toman." data-gr="כִּ֤י יַחְדָּ֨ו בֹּ֣קֶר לָ֣/מוֹ צַלְמָ֑וֶת כִּֽי יַ֝כִּ֗יר בַּלְה֥וֹת צַלְמָֽוֶת" data-lxx="ὅτι ὁμοθυμαδὸν τὸ πρωὶ αὐτοῖς σκιὰ θανάτου ὅτι ἐπιγνώσεται ταραχὰς σκιᾶς θανάτου" title="Porque la mañana es á todos ellos como sombra de muerte; Si son conocidos, terro…">Job 24:17</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="John 12:36" data-es="Entre tanto que tenéis la luz, creed en la luz, para que seáis hijos de luz. Estas cosas habló Jesús, y fuése, y escondióse de ellos." data-gr="⸀ὡς τὸ φῶς ἔχετε, πιστεύετε εἰς τὸ φῶς, ἵνα υἱοὶ φωτὸς γένησθε. Ταῦτα ⸀ἐλάλησεν Ἰησοῦς, καὶ ἀπελθὼν ἐκρύβη ἀπ’ αὐτῶν." data-lxx="" title="Entre tanto que tenéis la luz, creed en la luz, para que seáis hijos de luz. Est…">John 12:36</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="John 12:40" data-es="Cegó los ojos de ellos, y endureció su corazón; Porque no vean con los ojos, y entiendan de corazón, Y se conviertan, Y yo los sane." data-gr="Τετύφλωκεν αὐτῶν τοὺς ὀφθαλμοὺς καὶ ⸀ἐπώρωσεν αὐτῶν τὴν καρδίαν, ἵνα μὴ ἴδωσιν τοῖς ὀφθαλμοῖς καὶ νοήσωσιν τῇ καρδίᾳ καὶ ⸀στραφῶσιν, καὶ ⸀ἰάσομαι αὐτούς." data-lxx="" title="Cegó los ojos de ellos, y endureció su corazón; Porque no vean con los ojos, y e…">John 12:40</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="John 1:10" data-es="En el mundo estaba, y el mundo fué hecho por él; y el mundo no le conoció." data-gr="Ἐν τῷ κόσμῳ ἦν, καὶ ὁ κόσμος δι’ αὐτοῦ ἐγένετο, καὶ ὁ κόσμος αὐτὸν οὐκ ἔγνω." data-lxx="" title="En el mundo estaba, y el mundo fué hecho por él; y el mundo no le conoció.">John 1:10</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="John 3:19" data-es="Y esta es la condenación: porque la luz vino al mundo, y los hombres amaron más las tinieblas que la luz; porque sus obras eran malas." data-gr="αὕτη δέ ἐστιν ἡ κρίσις ὅτι τὸ φῶς ἐλήλυθεν εἰς τὸν κόσμον καὶ ἠγάπησαν οἱ ἄνθρωποι μᾶλλον τὸ σκότος ἢ τὸ φῶς, ἦν γὰρ ⸂αὐτῶν πονηρὰ⸃ τὰ ἔργα." data-lxx="" title="Y esta es la condenación: porque la luz vino al mundo, y los hombres amaron más …">John 3:19</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="John 3:20" data-es="Porque todo aquel que hace lo malo, aborrece la luz y no viene á la luz, porque sus obras no sean redargüidas." data-gr="πᾶς γὰρ ὁ φαῦλα πράσσων μισεῖ τὸ φῶς καὶ οὐκ ἔρχεται πρὸς τὸ φῶς, ἵνα μὴ ἐλεγχθῇ τὰ ἔργα αὐτοῦ·" data-lxx="" title="Porque todo aquel que hace lo malo, aborrece la luz y no viene á la luz, porque …">John 3:20</span></div><div id="pron-5" style="display:none;font-size:0.85rem;color:#1565c0;background:#e3f2fd;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;font-style:italic" class="pron-line"></div><div id="notes-5" style="display:none;margin-bottom:0.5rem"><textarea id="note-input-5" style="width:100%;min-height:50px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;padding:4px 8px;font-size:0.82rem;resize:vertical" placeholder="Tus notas para v.5..." oninput="saveNote(5)"></textarea></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-5')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="exeg-5" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">📜</span> Exégesis del Griego <span class="arrow" id="arrow-exeg-5">▶</span></div><div id="exeg-5" class="collapsed section-content exeg-section" role="region"><div class="exeg-summary"><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Alford:</strong> This φαίνει is not merely the historical present, but describes the whole process of the light of life in the Eternal Word shining in this evil and dark world; both by the O.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Bengel:</strong> αὐτὸ οὐ κατέλαβεν , [comprehended it not] did not attain to it ) Men, it seems, were too much averse from the Light, as well as too deeply sunk in darkness.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Robertson:</strong> This very phrase occurs in [John 12:35] ( ινα μη σκοτια υμας καταλαβη ) "that darkness overtake you not," the metaphor of night following day and in [1 Thessalonians 5:4] the same idiom ( ινα καταλαβη…<br></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv5_0').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Alford's Greek Testament</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1863)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv5_0" class="collapsed comm-body">5. ] As light and life are closely connected ideas, so are death and darkness . The whole world, lying in death and in darkness, is the σκοτία here spoken of: not merely the ἐσκοτωμένοι ([Ephesians 4:18] ; see ib. Eph 5:7-8 ), but the whole mass , with the sole exception (see below, Joh 1:12 ) of ὅσοι ἔλαβον αὐτόν (compare ch. [John 3:19] : 1Jn 5:19 ). This φαίνει is not merely the historical present, but describes the whole process of the light of life in the Eternal Word shining in this evil and dark world; both by the O.T. revelations, and (see ch. [John 10:16] ; Joh 11:52 ) by all the scattered fragments of light glittering among the thick darkness of heathendom. καὶ … κατέλ . ] and the darkness comprehended (understood, apprehended) it not . That this is the meaning, will be clear from the context. John states here as a general fact, what he afterwards states of the appearance of the Incarnate Word to the chosen people, [John 1:11] . The sentences are strictly parallel. τὸ φ . ἐν τῇ σκ . φαίνει [7] εἰς τὰ ἴδια ἦλθεν , and κ . ἡ σκ . αὐτὸ οὐ κατέλ . [8] καὶ οἱ ἴδιοι αὐτὸν οὐ παρέλαβον . In the first, he is speaking of the whole shining of this light over the world; in the second, of its historical manifestation to the Jews . In both cases, the Divine Word was rejected . παρέλαβον is used in the second case as expressing the personal assumption to oneself as a friend or companion: see reff. [7] When, in the Gospels, and in the Evangelic statement, [1 Corinthians 11:23-25] , the sign (║) occurs in a reference, it is signified that the word occurs in the parallel place in the other Gospels, which will always be found indicated at the head of the note on the paragraph. When the sign (║) is qualified , thus, &lsquo;║ Mk.,&rsquo; or &lsquo;║ Mt. Mk.,&rsquo; &c., it is signified that the word occurs in the parallel place in that Gospel or Gospels, but not in the other or others . [8] When, in the Gospels, and in the Evangelic statement, [1 Corinthians 11:23-25] , the sign (║) occurs in a reference, it is signified that the word occurs in the parallel place in the other Gospels, which will always be found indicated at the head of the note on the paragraph. When the sign (║) is qualified , thus, &lsquo;║ Mk.,&rsquo; or &lsquo;║ Mt. Mk.,&rsquo; &c., it is signified that the word occurs in the parallel place in that Gospel or Gospels, but not in the other or others . Lücke observes (i. 313), that the almost tragic tone of this verse is prevalent through the Gospel of John and his First Epistle, see ch. [John 3:19] ; [John 12:37] ff. alli [9] .: and is occasionally found in Paul also, see [Romans 1:18] ff. [9] alli = some cursive mss. The other interpretation of κατέλαβεν , &lsquo; overtook ,&rsquo; &lsquo; came upon &rsquo; (for that of &lsquo; overcame &rsquo; (Orig [10] , Theophyl., Euthym [11] ) is not admissible, the word never importing this), is unobjectionable as far as the usage of the word is concerned (see ch. [John 12:35] : Mar 9:18 ); but yi</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv5_1').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Bengel's Gnomon</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1742)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv5_1" class="collapsed comm-body">[John 1:5] . Καὶ , and ) From this verse the doctrine of evil and its rise, receives much light. ἐ τῇ σκοτίᾳ , in darkness ) This darkness is not said to be made. For it is a privation, which men have incurred [ To wit, that state of the human race is expressed by this word, which has prevailed since Adams transgression down to the appearance of the true Light . V. g.] It is in the darkness that the glory of the Light is the more conspicuously seen. φαίνει , shines ) The present time has the same force as in φωτίζει , [John 1:9] . It always φαίνει , shineth . The Light was always nigh at hand, even in the Old Testament, ready to apply a remedy to darkness and sin. The same word φαίνει , shineth , as regards the New Testament, [1 John 2:8] , &ldquo;The darkness is past, and the true light now shineth.&rdquo; καὶ οὐ , and not ) Similarly and not , [John 1:10-11] . ἡ σκοτία , the darkness ) i.e. men wrapt in darkness. αὐτὸ οὐ κατέλαβεν , [comprehended it not] did not attain to it ) Men, it seems, were too much averse from the Light, as well as too deeply sunk in darkness. When they did not comprehend the λόγον ἄσαρκον , The Word unclothed in flesh , &ldquo;He was made flesh,&rdquo; [John 1:14] .</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv5_2').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Robertson's Word Pictures</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1933)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv5_2" class="collapsed comm-body">Shineth ( φαινε ). Linear present active indicative of φαινω , old verb from φαω , to shine ( φαοσ, φως ). "The light keeps on giving light." In the darkness ( εν τη σκοτια ). Late word for the common σκοτος (kin to σκια , shadow). An evident allusion to the darkness brought on by sin. In [2 Peter 2:17] we have ο ζοφος του σκοτου (the blackness of darkness). The Logos, the only real moral light, keeps on shining both in the Pre-incarnate state and after the Incarnation. John is fond of σκοτια ( σκοτος ) for moral darkness from sin and φως ( φωτιζω, φαινω ) for the light that is in Christ alone. In [1 John 2:8] he proclaims that "the darkness is passing by and the true light is already shining." The Gnostics often employed these words and John takes them and puts them in the proper place. Apprehended it not ( αυτο ου κατελαβεν ). Second aorist active indicative of καταλαμβανω , old verb to lay hold of, to seize. This very phrase occurs in [John 12:35] ( ινα μη σκοτια υμας καταλαβη ) "that darkness overtake you not," the metaphor of night following day and in [1 Thessalonians 5:4] the same idiom ( ινα καταλαβη ) is used of day overtaking one as a thief. This is the view of Origen and appears also in 2Macc. 8:18. The same word appears in Aleph D in [John 6:17] κατελαβε δε αυτους η σκοτια ("but darkness overtook them," came down on them). Hence, in spite of the Vulgate comprehenderunt, "overtook" or "overcame" seems to be the idea here. The light kept on shining in spite of the darkness that was worse than a London fog as the Old Testament and archaeological discoveries in Egypt, Assyria, Babylonia, Persia, Crete, Asia Minor show.</div></div><div class="themes-divider">🔍 Temas discutidos</div><div class="theme-card"><div class="theme-word">κατέλαβεν</div><div class="consensus-bar"><div style="width:25%;background:#f44336"></div></div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#4caf50">✅ <strong>Alford</strong> κατέλαβεν significa 'comprendió' (entendió, aprehendió), no 'venció' - la oscuridad no lo comprendió.</div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#4caf50">✅ <strong>Robertson</strong> No se discute directamente el significado de κατέλαβεν en el texto proporcionado.</div><div class="theme-summary">Alford claramente favorece 'comprendió/entendió' sobre 'venció', pero falta discusión sustantiva de otros comentaristas para evaluar el consenso completo.</div></div></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('patr-5')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="patr-5" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">👨‍🏫</span> Patrística · 2 temas · 28 citas <span class="arrow" id="arrow-patr-5">▶</span></div><div id="patr-5" class="collapsed section-content patr-section" role="region"><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt652aa5b7').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>La Luz Brilla en las Tinieblas</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt652aa5b7" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (s.IV-V (354-430)) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.5]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Whereas that life is the light of men, but foolish hearts cannot receive that light, being so incumbered with sins that they cannot see it; for this cause lest any should think there is no light near them, because they cannot see it, he continues: And the light shineth in darkness, and the darkness comprehended it not. For suppose a blind man standing in the sun, the sun is present to him, but he is absent from the sun."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (s.IV (c.349-407)) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.5]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"And the light shineth in darkness. He calls death and error, darkness. For the light which is the object of our senses does not shine in darkness, but apart from it; but the preaching of Christ hath shone forth in the midst of prevailing error, and made it to disappear."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Gregory of Nazianzus</strong> (s.IV (329-390)) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Constantinopla, "el Teólogo" (Nacianzo)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorio_de_Nacianzo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.5]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"The light shines in darkness, in this life and in the flesh, and is chased by the darkness but is not overtaken by it. By this I mean the adverse power leaping up in its shamelessness against the visible Adam but encountering God and being defeated."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres concuerdan en que la luz divina brilla persistentemente en medio de las tinieblas del pecado, error y muerte. La luz no es vencida por las tinieblas sino que las supera.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pta66a677a').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Naturaleza de las Tinieblas</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pta66a677a" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> (s.V (c.376-444)) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Alejandría, Concilio de Éfeso (Alejandría)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cirilo_de_Alejandr%C3%ADa" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.5]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Darkness is what John calls the nature that lacks illumination, that is, the whole originate nature. For such a nature produces nothing on its own. Instead, it receives its whole being and well-being, such as it is, from its creator."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#ff9800"><div class="patr-cite-header">⚠️ <strong>Origen of Alexandria</strong> (s.III (c.185-254)) <span class="patr-meta">— Maestro catequético, exégeta, discípulo de Clemente de Alejandría (Alejandría/Cesarea)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Or%C3%ADgenes" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.5]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"People are not [darkness] by nature, since Paul says, For we were once darkness but now are light in the Lord, and this is especially the case if we are now called saints and spiritual. Just as Paul, although he was darkness, became capable of becoming light in the Lord, so may anyone who was once darkness."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Tatian the Assyrian</strong> (s.II (c.120-180)) <span class="patr-meta">— Apologista, discípulo de Justino Mártir (Siria)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taciano" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.5]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"The soul is not in itself immortal, O Greeks, but mortal. In itself it is darkness, and there is nothing luminous in it. And this is the meaning of the saying, The darkness comprehended it not."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Hay consenso en que las tinieblas representan la naturaleza creada carente de iluminación divina. Existe matiz sobre si esta condición es natural o resultado del pecado.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="verse-block" id="vb6"><div class="verse-header"><span class="vnum">6</span></div><div class="greek-line" id="greek-6">Ἐγένετο ἄνθρωπος ἀπεσταλμένος παρὰ Θεοῦ ὄνομα αὐτῷ Ἰωάννης</div><div class="uncial-line" id="uncial-6" style="display:none;font-family:'Noto Serif',serif;font-size:0.9rem;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#5d4037;background:#efebe9;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;overflow-wrap:break-word" title="Así se vería este versículo en un manuscrito uncial del siglo IV — todo mayúsculas, sin espacios (puntos medios añadidos como ayuda visual)">ΕΓΕΝΕΤΟ·ΑΝΘΡΩΠΟΣ·ΑΠΕΣΤΑΛΜΕΝΟΣ·ΠΑΡΑ·ΘΕΟΥ·ΟΝΟΜΑ·ΑΥΤΩΙ·ΙΩΑΝΝΗΣ<span style="display:block;font-size:0.65rem;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:0;opacity:0.7"><a href="https://www.codexsinaiticus.org/en/manuscript.aspx?book=33&chapter=1&verse=6" target="_blank" style="color:#5d4037">Ver en Codex Sinaiticus →</a></span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:0.3rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:0.3rem;align-items:center"><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="toggleRVR(6)">RVR60</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('uncial-6').style.display=document.getElementById('uncial-6').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#efebe9;color:#5d4037;border-color:#bcaaa4" title="Escritura uncial: así se veía el NT en los manuscritos del s.IV (Vaticanus, Sinaiticus). Todo mayúsculas, sin espacios entre palabras (scriptio continua), sin acentos ni puntuación. La iota subscrita se escribe explícitamente.">Uncial</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('pron-6').style.display=document.getElementById('pron-6').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0;border-color:#90caf9" title="Pronunciación bizantina aproximada (griego moderno/eclesiástico)">Pronunciación</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-patr" onclick="toggleSection('patr-6')" title="11 citas patrísticas disponibles">✝ 11 patrística</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-exeg" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-6')" title="3 comentarios exegéticos">📚 3 exégesis</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-ver" onclick="document.getElementById('vers-6').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="9 versiones disponibles">📖 versiones</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('xrefs-6').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="5 referencias cruzadas">🔗 5 refs</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="copyVerse(6)" title="Copiar versículo al portapapeles" style="background:#f3e5f5;border-color:#ce93d8;color:#6a1b9a">📋</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('notes-6').style.display=document.getElementById('notes-6').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" title="Notas personales" style="background:#fff8e1;border-color:#ffd54f;color:#f57f17">📝</div></div><div id="rvr-6" class="collapsed spanish-line">Hubo un hombre enviado de Dios, el cual se llamaba Juan.</div><div id="vers-6" class="collapsed" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR60</span>Hubo un hombre enviado de Dios, el cual se llamaba Juan.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR1909</span>Fué un hombre enviado de Dios, el cual se llamaba Juan.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">KJV</span>There was a man sent from God, whose name was John.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">ASV</span>There came a man, sent from God, whose name was John. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">BSB</span> There came a man who was sent from God. His name was John. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Darby</span>There was a man sent fromGod, his name John. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">LITV</span>There was a man sent from God; his name was John. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">YLT</span>There came a man--having been sent from God--whose name <FI>is<Fi> John,</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Vulgate</span>fuit homo missus a Deo cui nomen erat Iohannes</div></div><div id="xrefs-6" class="collapsed xref-container" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Isaiah 40:3" data-es="Voz que clama en el desierto: Barred camino á Jehová: enderezad calzada en la soledad á nuestro Dios." data-gr="ק֣וֹל קוֹרֵ֔א בַּ/מִּדְבָּ֕ר פַּנּ֖וּ דֶּ֣רֶךְ יְהוָ֑ה יַשְּׁרוּ֙ בָּ/עֲרָבָ֔ה מְסִלָּ֖ה לֵ/אלֹהֵֽי/נוּ" data-lxx="φωνὴ βοῶντος ἐν τῇ ἐρήμῳ ἑτοιμάσατε τὴν ὁδὸν κυρίου εὐθείας ποιεῖτε τὰς τρίβους τοῦ θεοῦ ἡμῶν" title="Voz que clama en el desierto: Barred camino á Jehová: enderezad calzada en la so…">Isaiah 40:3</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Isaiah 40:5" data-es="Y manifestaráse la gloria de Jehová, y toda carne juntamente la verá; que la boca de Jehová habló." data-gr="וְ/נִגְלָ֖ה כְּב֣וֹד יְהוָ֑ה וְ/רָא֤וּ כָל בָּשָׂר֙ יַחְדָּ֔ו כִּ֛י פִּ֥י יְהוָ֖ה דִּבֵּֽר" data-lxx="καὶ ὀφθήσεται ἡ δόξα κυρίου καὶ ὄψεται πᾶσα σὰρξ τὸ σωτήριον τοῦ θεοῦ ὅτι κύριος ἐλάλησεν" title="Y manifestaráse la gloria de Jehová, y toda carne juntamente la verá; que la boc…">Isaiah 40:5</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="John 1:33" data-es="Y yo no le conocía; mas el que me envió á bautizar con agua, aquél me dijo: Sobre quien vieres descender el Espíritu, y que reposa sobre él, éste es el que bautiza con Espíritu Santo." data-gr="κἀγὼ οὐκ ᾔδειν αὐτόν, ἀλλ’ ὁ πέμψας με βαπτίζειν ἐν ὕδατι ἐκεῖνός μοι εἶπεν· Ἐφ’ ὃν ἂν ἴδῃς τὸ πνεῦμα καταβαῖνον καὶ μένον ἐπ’ αὐτόν, οὗτός ἐστιν ὁ βαπτίζων ἐν πνεύματι ἁγίῳ·" data-lxx="" title="Y yo no le conocía; mas el que me envió á bautizar con agua, aquél me dijo: Sobr…">John 1:33</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="John 3:28" data-es="Vosotros mismos me sois testigos que dije: Yo no soy el Cristo, sino que soy enviado delante de él." data-gr="αὐτοὶ ὑμεῖς ⸀μοι μαρτυρεῖτε ὅτι ⸀εἶπον· Οὐκ εἰμὶ ἐγὼ ὁ χριστός, ἀλλ’ ὅτι Ἀπεσταλμένος εἰμὶ ἔμπροσθεν ἐκείνου." data-lxx="" title="Vosotros mismos me sois testigos que dije: Yo no soy el Cristo, sino que soy env…">John 3:28</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Malachi 3:1" data-es="HE aquí, yo envío mi mensajero, el cual preparará el camino delante de mí: y luego vendrá á su templo el Señor á quien vosotros buscáis, y el ángel del pacto, á quien deseáis vosotros. He aquí viene, ha dicho Jehová de los ejércitos." data-gr="הִנְ/נִ֤י שֹׁלֵחַ֙ מַלְאָכִ֔/י וּ/פִנָּה דֶ֖רֶךְ לְ/פָנָ֑/י וּ/פִתְאֹם֩ יָב֨וֹא אֶל הֵיכָל֜/וֹ הָ/אָד֣וֹן אֲשֶׁר אַתֶּ֣ם מְבַקְשִׁ֗ים וּ/מַלְאַ֨ךְ הַ/בְּרִ֜ית אֲשֶׁר אַתֶּ֤ם חֲפֵצִים֙ הִנֵּה בָ֔א אָמַ֖ר יְהוָ֥ה צְבָאֽוֹת" data-lxx="ἰδοὺ ἐγὼ ἐξαποστέλλω τὸν ἄγγελόν μου καὶ ἐπιβλέψεται ὁδὸν πρὸ προσώπου μου καὶ ἐξαίφνης ἥξει εἰς τὸν ναὸν ἑαυτοῦ κύριος ὃν ὑμεῖς ζητεῖτε καὶ ὁ ἄγγελος τῆς διαθήκης ὃν ὑμεῖς θέλετε ἰδοὺ ἔρχεται λέγει κύριος παντοκράτωρ" title="HE aquí, yo envío mi mensajero, el cual preparará el camino delante de mí: y lue…">Malachi 3:1</span></div><div id="pron-6" style="display:none;font-size:0.85rem;color:#1565c0;background:#e3f2fd;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;font-style:italic" class="pron-line"></div><div id="notes-6" style="display:none;margin-bottom:0.5rem"><textarea id="note-input-6" style="width:100%;min-height:50px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;padding:4px 8px;font-size:0.82rem;resize:vertical" placeholder="Tus notas para v.6..." oninput="saveNote(6)"></textarea></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-6')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="exeg-6" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">📜</span> Exégesis del Griego <span class="arrow" id="arrow-exeg-6">▶</span></div><div id="exeg-6" class="collapsed section-content exeg-section" role="region"><div class="exeg-summary"><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Alford:</strong> μετεληλυθὼς ἐπὶ τὴν ἐπιφάνειαν τοῦ υἱοῦ , τίνα ἂν εὗρεν ἀρχὴν ἑτέραν , ἢ τὰ κατὰ τὸν Ἰωάννην ; (Theodor.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Bengel:</strong> ἄνθρωπος , a man ) God deals with men through agents similar to themselves, namely, men; in order that they may the more readily take [&lsquo;capiant,&rsquo; take in, understand] and accept [His offer…<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Robertson:</strong> There came a man ( εγενετο ανθρωπος ).<br></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv6_0').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Alford's Greek Testament</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1863)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv6_0" class="collapsed comm-body">6. ] The Evangelist now passes to the historic manifestation of the Word. μετεληλυθὼς ἐπὶ τὴν ἐπιφάνειαν τοῦ υἱοῦ , τίνα ἂν εὗρεν ἀρχὴν ἑτέραν , ἢ τὰ κατὰ τὸν Ἰωάννην ; (Theodor. Mopsuest [12] in loc. p. 729, ed. Migne.) He enunciates briefly in these [John 1:6-7] , what he afterwards, [John 1:19-36] , narrates with historical detail. [12] Mopsuest. Theodore, Bp. of Mopsuestia, 399 428 ἐγένετο not belonging to ἀπεσταλμένος , but to ἄνθρ .: the ordinary opening of an historical period, see [Luke 1:5] . No stress on ἐγένετο , as distinguished from ἦν , [John 1:1] (Olshausen), see ch. [John 3:1] . There was a man sent, &c. In ἀπεστ . παρὰ θεοῦ we have possibly a reference to [Malachi 3:1] .</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv6_1').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Bengel's Gnomon</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1742)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv6_1" class="collapsed comm-body">[John 1:6] . Ἐγένετο ) not ἦν . The Evangelist does not say, was of John, but was made [fiebat: εἶναι is to be , γίνεσθαι , to begin to be ]. The question is asked, how far the opening introduction to this book extends. The answer is. There is no introduction: the treatise itself [ipsa tractatio, the handling of the subject itself] begins with the beginning of the book. For in Joh 1:6 the Evangelist already describes the office of John, in bearing witness of the Light: and in the first five verses, he records what before had always been the nature and principle of the Light. Therefore up to this point a summary has been given of those things, which evidently preceded John; nor can these by any means be referred to the action of Jesus immediately succeeding John, as Artemonius, p. 412, refers it; and now there is unfolded by the Evangelist a more copious description of recent [new] events. Both [the things preceding John, and the things then from that point occurring] are most orderly in their arrangement. ἄνθρωπος , a man ) God deals with men through agents similar to themselves, namely, men; in order that they may the more readily take [&lsquo;capiant,&rsquo; take in, understand] and accept [His offers of love]. ἀπεσταλμένος παρὰ Θεοῦ , sent from God ) The definition of a prophet. Comp. [Matthew 11:9-10] [A prophet? Yea and more than a prophet. For this is He, of whom it is written, Behold I send My messenger ,&rdquo; etc.] The Participle is here in immediate connection with the noun a man : and in mediate connection with the verb, was made [ ἐγένετο began to be]. παρὰ Θεοῦ , from God , [John 1:33] . Ἰωάννης , John ) That is, an interpreter [exponent] of the grace of God . The greatness of John [is hereby implied], of whom mention is made immediately after the preceding statements [ Joh 1:1-5 ]. Greater knowledge was brought into the world through John, than had been in all previous ages.</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv6_2').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Robertson's Word Pictures</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1933)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv6_2" class="collapsed comm-body">There came a man ( εγενετο ανθρωπος ). Definite event in the long darkness, same verb in verse [John 1:3]. Sent ( απεσταλμενος ). Perfect passive participle of αποστελλω , to send. From God ( παρα θεου ). From the side of ( παρα ) God (ablative case θεου ). Whose name ( ονομα αυτω ). "Name to him," nominative parenthetic and dative (Robertson, Grammar, p. 460). John ( Ιωανης ). One ν in Westcott and Hort. In the giving of the name see [Luke 1:59-63], Hellenized form of Jonathan, Joanan (Gift of God), used always of the Baptist in this Gospel which never mentions the name of John son of Zebedee (the sons of Zebedee once, [John 21:2]).</div></div></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('patr-6')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="patr-6" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">👨‍🏫</span> Patrística · 2 temas · 11 citas <span class="arrow" id="arrow-patr-6">▶</span></div><div id="patr-6" class="collapsed section-content patr-section" role="region"><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt75579d9e').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Juan el Bautista como precursor enviado por Dios</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt75579d9e" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Irenaeus</strong> (c.130-202) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Lyon, mártir, discípulo de Policarpo (discípulo de Juan) (Lyon)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ireneo_de_Lyon" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.6]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"And that we may not have to ask, Of what God was the Word made flesh? he does himself previously teach us, saying, 'There was a man sent from God, whose name was John. The same came as a witness, that he might bear witness of that Light. He was not that Light, but [came] that he might testify of the Light.' By what God, then, was John, the forerunner, who testifies of the Light, sent [into the world]?"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.6]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"There was a man sent from God whose name was John. Truly, brethren beloved, those things which were said before, were said regarding the ineffable divinity of Christ, and almost ineffably. For who shall comprehend 'In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God'?"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.6]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Having in the introduction spoken to us things of urgent importance concerning God the Word, (the Evangelist) proceeding on his road, and in order, afterwards comes to the herald of the Word, his namesake John. And now that thou hearest that he was 'sent from God,' do not for the future imagine that any of the words spoken by him are mere man's words; for all that he utters is not his own, but is of Him who sent him."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Jerome</strong> (c.347-420) <span class="patr-meta">— Traductor de la Vulgata, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Gregorio de Nacianzo (Belén)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jer%C3%B3nimo_de_Estrid%C3%B3n" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.6]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Where we say 'sent,' the Hebrew says, 'one sent forth'; in Greek apostolos, in Hebrew siloas. You see, therefore, that this John, the prophet, is not only a prophet but also an apostle. Isaiah is sent; he was an apostle. 'Here I am, send me!' 'Sent' is a term well said.… Those who have come on their own authority and have not been sent are the thieves and robbers."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres están unánimes en que Juan el Bautista fue enviado por Dios como precursor y heraldo del Verbo. Su autoridad deriva de ser enviado por Dios, no de sí mismo.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt4bc76520').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Juan el Bautista como testigo de la Luz</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt4bc76520" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> (c.376-444) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Alejandría, Concilio de Éfeso (Alejandría)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cirilo_de_Alejandr%C3%ADa" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.6]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Having before Explained about God the Word, and most accurately gone through the things whereby He is shown to be by Nature Son of God the Father, he fortifies their faith in what they had already heard by his words. And since (according to what was said by God through Moses), At the mouth of two and three witnesses shall every word be established, wisely does he bring in addition to himself the blessed Baptist, and introduces him along with himself a most noteworthy witness."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.7]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Therefore, because He was so man, that the God lay hid in Him, there was sent before Him a great man, by whose testimony He might be found to be more than man. And who is this? 'He was a man.' And how could that man speak the truth concerning God? 'He was sent by God.' What was he called? 'Whose name was John.' Wherefore did he come? 'He came for a witness, that he might bear witness concerning the light, that all might believe through him.'"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.7]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"The same came for a witness, to bear witness of that Light. What is this, perhaps one may say, the servant bear witness to his Master? When then you see Him not only witnessed to by His servant, but even coming to him, and with Jews baptized by him, will you not be still more astonished and perplexed? Yet you ought not to be troubled nor confused, but amazed at such unspeakable goodness..."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres concuerdan en que Juan vino específicamente como testigo de Cristo, la Luz verdadera. Su testimonio era necesario para que los hombres reconocieran la divinidad oculta de Cristo.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="verse-block" id="vb7"><div class="verse-header"><span class="vnum">7</span></div><div class="greek-line" id="greek-7">οὗτος ἦλθεν εἰς μαρτυρίαν ἵνα μαρτυρήσῃ περὶ τοῦ φωτός ἵνα πάντες πιστεύσωσιν δι᾽ αὐτοῦ</div><div class="uncial-line" id="uncial-7" style="display:none;font-family:'Noto Serif',serif;font-size:0.9rem;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#5d4037;background:#efebe9;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;overflow-wrap:break-word" title="Así se vería este versículo en un manuscrito uncial del siglo IV — todo mayúsculas, sin espacios (puntos medios añadidos como ayuda visual)">ΟΥΤΟΣ·ΗΛΘΕΝ·ΕΙΣ·ΜΑΡΤΥΡΙΑΝ·ΙΝΑ·ΜΑΡΤΥΡΗΣΗΙ·ΠΕΡΙ·ΤΟΥ·ΦΩΤΟΣ·ΙΝΑ·ΠΑΝΤΕΣ·ΠΙΣΤΕΥΣΩΣΙΝ·ΔΙ·ΑΥΤΟΥ<span style="display:block;font-size:0.65rem;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:0;opacity:0.7"><a href="https://www.codexsinaiticus.org/en/manuscript.aspx?book=33&chapter=1&verse=7" target="_blank" style="color:#5d4037">Ver en Codex Sinaiticus →</a></span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:0.3rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:0.3rem;align-items:center"><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="toggleRVR(7)">RVR60</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('uncial-7').style.display=document.getElementById('uncial-7').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#efebe9;color:#5d4037;border-color:#bcaaa4" title="Escritura uncial: así se veía el NT en los manuscritos del s.IV (Vaticanus, Sinaiticus). Todo mayúsculas, sin espacios entre palabras (scriptio continua), sin acentos ni puntuación. La iota subscrita se escribe explícitamente.">Uncial</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('pron-7').style.display=document.getElementById('pron-7').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0;border-color:#90caf9" title="Pronunciación bizantina aproximada (griego moderno/eclesiástico)">Pronunciación</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-patr" onclick="toggleSection('patr-7')" title="10 citas patrísticas disponibles">✝ 10 patrística</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-exeg" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-7')" title="3 comentarios exegéticos">📚 3 exégesis</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-ver" onclick="document.getElementById('vers-7').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="9 versiones disponibles">📖 versiones</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('xrefs-7').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="1 referencias cruzadas">🔗 1 refs</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="copyVerse(7)" title="Copiar versículo al portapapeles" style="background:#f3e5f5;border-color:#ce93d8;color:#6a1b9a">📋</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('notes-7').style.display=document.getElementById('notes-7').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" title="Notas personales" style="background:#fff8e1;border-color:#ffd54f;color:#f57f17">📝</div></div><div id="rvr-7" class="collapsed spanish-line">Este vino por testimonio, para que diese testimonio de la luz, a fin de que todos creyesen por él.</div><div id="vers-7" class="collapsed" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR60</span>Este vino por testimonio, para que diese testimonio de la luz, a fin de que todos creyesen por él.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR1909</span>Este vino por testimonio, para que diese testimonio de la luz, para que todos creyesen por él.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">KJV</span>The same came for a witness, to bear witness of the Light, that all men through him might believe.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">ASV</span>The same came for witness, that he might bear witness of the light, that all might believe through him. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">BSB</span>He came as a witness to testify about the Light, so that through him everyone might believe. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Darby</span>He came for witness, that he might witness concerning the light, that all might believe through him. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">LITV</span>He came for a witness, that he might witness concerning the Light, that all might believe through Him. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">YLT</span>this one came for testimony, that he might testify about the Light, that all might believe through him;</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Vulgate</span>hic venit in testimonium ut testimonium perhiberet de lumine ut omnes crederent per illum</div></div><div id="xrefs-7" class="collapsed xref-container" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Acts 19:4" data-es="Y dijo Pablo: Juan bautizó con bautismo de arrepentimiento, diciendo al pueblo que creyesen en el que había de venir después de él, es á saber, en Jesús el Cristo." data-gr="εἶπεν δὲ Παῦλος· ⸀Ἰωάννης ἐβάπτισεν βάπτισμα μετανοίας, τῷ λαῷ λέγων εἰς τὸν ἐρχόμενον μετ’ αὐτὸν ἵνα πιστεύσωσιν, τοῦτ’ ἔστιν εἰς ⸀τὸν Ἰησοῦν." data-lxx="" title="Y dijo Pablo: Juan bautizó con bautismo de arrepentimiento, diciendo al pueblo q…">Acts 19:4</span></div><div id="pron-7" style="display:none;font-size:0.85rem;color:#1565c0;background:#e3f2fd;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;font-style:italic" class="pron-line"></div><div id="notes-7" style="display:none;margin-bottom:0.5rem"><textarea id="note-input-7" style="width:100%;min-height:50px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;padding:4px 8px;font-size:0.82rem;resize:vertical" placeholder="Tus notas para v.7..." oninput="saveNote(7)"></textarea></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-7')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="exeg-7" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">📜</span> Exégesis del Griego <span class="arrow" id="arrow-exeg-7">▶</span></div><div id="exeg-7" class="collapsed section-content exeg-section" role="region"><div class="exeg-summary"><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Alford:</strong> εἰς μαρτυρίαν , not as E.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Bengel:</strong> ] [14] May it not express the grace of God, &ldquo;who will, θέλει , have all men to be saved and to come to the knowledge of the truth,&rdquo; [1 Timothy 2:4].<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Robertson:</strong> For witness ( εις μαρτυριαν ).<br></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv7_0').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Alford's Greek Testament</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1863)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv7_0" class="collapsed comm-body">7. ] The purpose of John&rsquo;s coming was to bear witness to a fact , which fact ( Joh 1:33 ) was made known to him by divine revelation. εἰς μαρτυρίαν , not as E. V., &lsquo; for a witness ,&rsquo; but for witness, for the purpose of bearing witness: so A.V.R. ἵνα μαρτ . κ . τ . λ . is an expansion of εἰς μαρτ . : the subject of his testimony was to be the Light , and the aim of it, that all might believe ( εἰς τὸ φῶς , see ch. Joh 12:36 ) through him (i.e. John: not τοῦ φωτός (Grot.), which confuses the whole, for then we must understand εἰς θεόν after πιστ . which is here out of place).</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv7_1').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Bengel's Gnomon</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1742)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv7_1" class="collapsed comm-body">[John 1:7] . Εἰς μαρτυρίαν , for a witness ) The evangelist again touches on this, [John 1:15] , and again, [John 1:19] . But with the fullest and most tender feeling he interweaves with this testimony of the Forerunner his own testimony as an apostle, by means of most noble digressions, in which he states the nature and grounds of the Baptist&rsquo;s office, and partly premises, partly subjoins an explanation of his [the Baptist&rsquo;s] brief sentences, and declares the full complement of his testimony [gives a clear filling up of it]: [ thus forming a kind of succinct prelude to our Lord&rsquo;s own speeches, which He was about to set forth in this very Gospel. Harm. , p. 153.] What Matthew, Mark, and Luke term a Gospel , this John for the most part terms a testimony or witness : the former term expresses the relation to the promise, that went before: the latter expresses the altogether certain knowledge of him, who announces it: the former is used in reference to Christ as He was manifested; the latter, with reference to the Glory of Jesus Christ, the Son of GOD, when raised from the dead: accordingly, in the Acts and Epistles of the Apostles, both are often employed. Testimony applies to a thing, known for certain by witnesses, a thing not falling under the eyes at least of the hearers, and yet all important to them: accordingly to it answers faith . There follows immediately the declaration, that he might bear witness of the Light : and the words, that he might bear witness , are handled forthwith: the words, of the Light , are handled at [John 1:9] . ἳνα μαρτυρήσῃ , that he might bear witness ) The sum of his testimony was: He, who comes after me , etc., [John 1:15] . περί τοῦ Θωτός , concerning the Light ) John comprises under the appellation of the Light , the things which he wrote, [John 1:1-5] . ἳνα , in order that ) They need Testimony, who were in darkness. πάντες , all men ) to whom He had come . [14] ΔἸ ΑὐΤΟῦ , through him ) through John, not εἰς αὐτόν , not in John, but in Christ, [John 1:12] . [15] The power of John&rsquo;s testimony extended itself so as even to come under the knowledge of the Gentiles, [Acts 10:37] [Peter addressing the Gentiles , Cornelius and others, &ldquo;That word ye know , which was published throughout all Judea, etc., after the baptism, which John preached.&rdquo;] Διά , through , in a higher sense, is said of Christ, [1 Peter 1:21] [Who by Him do believe in God.] [14] May it not express the grace of God, &ldquo;who will, θέλει , have all men to be saved and to come to the knowledge of the truth,&rdquo; [1 Timothy 2:4] . E. [15] Grot. wrongly understands διʼ αὐτοῦ through Him, the Light, which would confuse the whole, by rendering it necessary to understand εἰς θεόν after πιστεύσωσι . E.</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv7_2').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Robertson's Word Pictures</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1933)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv7_2" class="collapsed comm-body">For witness ( εις μαρτυριαν ). Old word from μαρτυρεω (from μαρτυς ), both more common in John's writings than the rest of the N.T. This the purpose of the Baptist's ministry. That he might bear witness ( ινα μαρτυρηση ). Final clause with ινα and aorist active subjunctive of μαρτυρεω to make clearer εις μαρτυριαν . Of the light ( περ του φωτος ). "Concerning the light." The light was shining and men with blinded eyes were not seeing the light ([John 1:26]), blinded by the god of this world still ([2 Corinthians 4:4]). John had his own eyes opened so that he saw and told what he saw. That is the mission of every preacher of Christ. But he must first have his own eyes opened. That all might believe ( ινα πιστευσωσιν ). Final clause with ινα and first aorist active subjunctive of πιστευω , ingressive aorist "come to believe." This is one of John's great words (about 100 times), "with nine times the frequency with which it is used by the Synoptists" (Bernard). And yet πιστις , so common in Paul, John uses only in [1 John 5:4] and four times in the Apocalypse where πιστευω does not occur at all. Here it is used absolutely as in [John 1:50], etc. Through him ( δι' αυτου ). As the intermediate agent in winning men to believe in Christ (the Logos) as the Light and the Life of men. This is likewise the purpose of the author of this book ([John 21:31]). The preacher is merely the herald to point men to Christ.</div></div></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('patr-7')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="patr-7" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">👨‍🏫</span> Patrística · 2 temas · 10 citas <span class="arrow" id="arrow-patr-7">▶</span></div><div id="patr-7" class="collapsed section-content patr-section" role="region"><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('ptd871eb1e').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Juan el Bautista como testigo de la Luz</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="ptd871eb1e" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> (c.376-444) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Alejandría, Concilio de Éfeso (Alejandría)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cirilo_de_Alejandr%C3%ADa" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.6]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Having before Explained about God the Word, and most accurately gone through the things whereby He is shown to be by Nature Son of God the Father, he fortifies their faith in what they had already heard by his words. And since (according to what was said by God through Moses), At the mouth of two and three witnesses shall every word be established, wisely does he bring in addition to himself the blessed Baptist, and introduces him along with himself a most noteworthy witness."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.7]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Therefore, because He was so man, that the God lay hid in Him, there was sent before Him a great man, by whose testimony He might be found to be more than man. And who is this? 'He was a man.' And how could that man speak the truth concerning God? 'He was sent by God.' What was he called? 'Whose name was John.' Wherefore did he come? 'He came for a witness, that he might bear witness concerning the light, that all might believe through him.'"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.7]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"The same came for a witness, to bear witness of that Light. What is this, perhaps one may say, the servant bear witness to his Master? When then you see Him not only witnessed to by His servant, but even coming to him, and with Jews baptized by him, will you not be still more astonished and perplexed? Yet you ought not to be troubled nor confused, but amazed at such unspeakable goodness..."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres concuerdan en que Juan vino específicamente como testigo de Cristo, la Luz verdadera. Su testimonio era necesario para que los hombres reconocieran la divinidad oculta de Cristo.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt812f5044').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>La necesidad del testimonio profético</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:55%;background:#ff9800"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#ff9800">medio</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt812f5044" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Origen of Alexandria</strong> (c.185-254) <span class="patr-meta">— Maestro catequético, exégeta, discípulo de Clemente de Alejandría (Alejandría/Cesarea)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Or%C3%ADgenes" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.7]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Some try to undo the testimonies of the prophets to Christ by saying that the Son of God had no need of such witnesses.… To this we may reply that where there are a number of reasons to make people believe, persons are often impressed by one kind of proof and not by another.And with respect to the doctrine of the incarnation, it is certain that some have been forced by the prophetical writings into an admiration of Christ"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> (c.376-444) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Alejandría, Concilio de Éfeso (Alejandría)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cirilo_de_Alejandr%C3%ADa" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.7]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Since, according to what was said by God through Moses, 'At the mouth of two and three witnesses shall every word be established,' wisely does [John the Evangelist] bring in addition to himself the blessed Baptist.… For he did not suppose that he ought, even if of gravest weight, to demand of the readers in his book concerning our Savior credence above that of the law, and that they should believe him by himself when declaring things above our understanding and sense."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Algunos Padres defienden la necesidad del testimonio profético contra objeciones de que Cristo no necesitaba testigos. Argumentan que Dios provee múltiples formas de evidencia para diferentes tipos de personas.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="verse-block" id="vb8"><div class="verse-header"><span class="vnum">8</span></div><div class="greek-line" id="greek-8">οὐκ ἦν ἐκεῖνος τὸ φῶς ἀλλ᾽ ἵνα μαρτυρήσῃ περὶ τοῦ φωτός</div><div class="uncial-line" id="uncial-8" style="display:none;font-family:'Noto Serif',serif;font-size:0.9rem;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#5d4037;background:#efebe9;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;overflow-wrap:break-word" title="Así se vería este versículo en un manuscrito uncial del siglo IV — todo mayúsculas, sin espacios (puntos medios añadidos como ayuda visual)">ΟΥΚ·ΗΝ·ΕΚΕΙΝΟΣ·ΤΟ·ΦΩΣ·ΑΛΛ·ΙΝΑ·ΜΑΡΤΥΡΗΣΗΙ·ΠΕΡΙ·ΤΟΥ·ΦΩΤΟΣ<span style="display:block;font-size:0.65rem;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:0;opacity:0.7"><a href="https://www.codexsinaiticus.org/en/manuscript.aspx?book=33&chapter=1&verse=8" target="_blank" style="color:#5d4037">Ver en Codex Sinaiticus →</a></span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:0.3rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:0.3rem;align-items:center"><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="toggleRVR(8)">RVR60</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('uncial-8').style.display=document.getElementById('uncial-8').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#efebe9;color:#5d4037;border-color:#bcaaa4" title="Escritura uncial: así se veía el NT en los manuscritos del s.IV (Vaticanus, Sinaiticus). Todo mayúsculas, sin espacios entre palabras (scriptio continua), sin acentos ni puntuación. La iota subscrita se escribe explícitamente.">Uncial</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('pron-8').style.display=document.getElementById('pron-8').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0;border-color:#90caf9" title="Pronunciación bizantina aproximada (griego moderno/eclesiástico)">Pronunciación</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-patr" onclick="toggleSection('patr-8')" title="16 citas patrísticas disponibles">✝ 16 patrística</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-exeg" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-8')" title="3 comentarios exegéticos">📚 3 exégesis</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-ver" onclick="document.getElementById('vers-8').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="9 versiones disponibles">📖 versiones</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('xrefs-8').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="2 referencias cruzadas">🔗 2 refs</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="copyVerse(8)" title="Copiar versículo al portapapeles" style="background:#f3e5f5;border-color:#ce93d8;color:#6a1b9a">📋</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('notes-8').style.display=document.getElementById('notes-8').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" title="Notas personales" style="background:#fff8e1;border-color:#ffd54f;color:#f57f17">📝</div></div><div id="rvr-8" class="collapsed spanish-line">No era él la luz, sino para que diese testimonio de la luz.</div><div id="vers-8" class="collapsed" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR60</span>No era él la luz, sino para que diese testimonio de la luz.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR1909</span>No era él la luz, sino para que diese testimonio de la luz.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">KJV</span>He was not that Light, but was sent to bear witness of that Light.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">ASV</span>He was not the light, but came that he might bear witness of the light. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">BSB</span>He himself was not the Light, but he came to testify about the Light. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Darby</span>He was not the light, but that he might witness concerning the light. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">LITV</span>He was not that Light, but that he might witness concerning the Light. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">YLT</span>that one was not the Light, but--that he might testify about the Light.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Vulgate</span>non erat ille lux sed ut testimonium perhiberet de lumine</div></div><div id="xrefs-8" class="collapsed xref-container" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="John 1:20" data-es="Y confesó, y no negó; mas declaró: No soy yo el Cristo." data-gr="καὶ ὡμολόγησεν καὶ οὐκ ἠρνήσατο, καὶ ὡμολόγησεν ὅτι ⸂Ἐγὼ οὐκ εἰμὶ⸃ ὁ χριστός." data-lxx="" title="Y confesó, y no negó; mas declaró: No soy yo el Cristo.">John 1:20</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="John 3:28" data-es="Vosotros mismos me sois testigos que dije: Yo no soy el Cristo, sino que soy enviado delante de él." data-gr="αὐτοὶ ὑμεῖς ⸀μοι μαρτυρεῖτε ὅτι ⸀εἶπον· Οὐκ εἰμὶ ἐγὼ ὁ χριστός, ἀλλ’ ὅτι Ἀπεσταλμένος εἰμὶ ἔμπροσθεν ἐκείνου." data-lxx="" title="Vosotros mismos me sois testigos que dije: Yo no soy el Cristo, sino que soy env…">John 3:28</span></div><div id="pron-8" style="display:none;font-size:0.85rem;color:#1565c0;background:#e3f2fd;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;font-style:italic" class="pron-line"></div><div id="notes-8" style="display:none;margin-bottom:0.5rem"><textarea id="note-input-8" style="width:100%;min-height:50px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;padding:4px 8px;font-size:0.82rem;resize:vertical" placeholder="Tus notas para v.8..." oninput="saveNote(8)"></textarea></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-8')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="exeg-8" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">📜</span> Exégesis del Griego <span class="arrow" id="arrow-exeg-8">▶</span></div><div id="exeg-8" class="collapsed section-content exeg-section" role="region"><div class="exeg-summary"><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Alford:</strong> ] John was himself ὁ λύχνος ὁ καιόμενος καὶ φαίνων (ch.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Bengel:</strong> Ἐκεῖνος , That One ) Some had suspected, that John was the Light: ἐκεῖνος , that One points out a more remote object.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Robertson:</strong> He was a light ([John 5:35]) as all believers are ([Matthew 5:14]), but not "the light" ( το φως ).<br></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv8_0').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Alford's Greek Testament</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1863)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv8_0" class="collapsed comm-body">8. ] John was himself ὁ λύχνος ὁ καιόμενος καὶ φαίνων (ch. Joh 5:35 ), see note on [Matthew 5:14] , but not τὸ φῶς . On ἵνα , see reff.: it belongs to ἦν , not to ἦλθεν above. And thus there is no ellipsis of &lsquo; came &rsquo; or &lsquo;was sent:&rsquo; John simply was , in order to &c.</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv8_1').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Bengel's Gnomon</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1742)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv8_1" class="collapsed comm-body">[John 1:8] . Ἐκεῖνος , That One ) Some had suspected, that John was the Light: ἐκεῖνος , that One points out a more remote object.</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv8_2').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Robertson's Word Pictures</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1933)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv8_2" class="collapsed comm-body">He ( εκεινος ). "That one," i.e. John. He was a light ([John 5:35]) as all believers are ([Matthew 5:14]), but not "the light" ( το φως ). But came ( αλλ' ). No verb in the Greek, to be supplied by repeating ηλθεν of verse [John 1:7]. See similar ellipses in [John 9:3]; [John 13:18]; [John 15:25]. In Johannine fashion we have the final ινα clause of verse [John 1:7] repeated.</div></div></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('patr-8')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="patr-8" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">👨‍🏫</span> Patrística · 3 temas · 16 citas <span class="arrow" id="arrow-patr-8">▶</span></div><div id="patr-8" class="collapsed section-content patr-section" role="region"><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('ptb7d9bb93').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Juan el Bautista no es la Luz verdadera</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="ptb7d9bb93" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.8]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"How right it was for the Lord to call [John] a lamp. This is what the Lord said about John: 'He was a burning and a shining lamp, and you were willing for a time to exult in his light.' What, though, does John the Evangelist say about him? 'There was a man sent by God, whose name was John; this man came for witness, to bear witness about the light; that man was not the light.' Who? John the Baptist. Who says this? John the Evangelist. 'That man was not the light.'"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.8]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"He was not that Light. Now if he did not introduce this as setting himself against this suspicion, then the expression is absolutely superfluous, and tautology rather than elucidation of his teaching. For why, after having said that he 'was sent to bear witness of that Light,' does he again say, 'He was not that Light'? (He says it,) not loosely or without reason; but, because, for the most part, among ourselves, the person witnessing is held to be greater, and generally more trustworthy than"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> (c.376-444) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Alejandría, Concilio de Éfeso (Alejandría)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cirilo_de_Alejandr%C3%ADa" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.8]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"The Baptist having esteemed desert-abodes above the haunts of the cities, and having shown forth an unwonted persistence in exercise of virtue, and having mounted to the very summit of the righteousness attainable by man, was most rightly wondered at, and even by some imagined to be Christ Himself. And indeed the rulers of the Jews led by his achievements in virtue to some such notion, send some to him bidding them to inquire if he be the Christ."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres enfatizan que Juan no era la Luz verdadera sino solo un testigo de ella. Esta aclaración era necesaria porque algunos confundían a Juan con el Cristo debido a su gran virtud.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pte91b3247').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Distinción entre luz creada y Luz increada</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pte91b3247" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.8]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Wherefore then did he come? 'But that he might bear witness concerning the light.' Why so? 'That all might believe through him.' And concerning what light was he to bear witness? 'That was the true light.' Wherefore is it added true? Because an enlightened man is also called a light; but the true light is that which enlightens. For even our eyes are called lights; and nevertheless, unless either during the night a lamp is lighted, or during the day the sun goes forth, these lights are open in vain."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.8]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"John, a man of distinguished grace, was sent before Him, a man enlightened by Him who is the Light. For of John it is said, 'He was not the Light, but that he should bear witness of the Light.' He may himself be called a light indeed, and rightly so; but an enlightened, not an enlightening light. The light that enlightens, and that which is enlightened, are different things: for even our eyes are called lights, and yet when we open them in the dark, they do not see."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> (c.376-444) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Alejandría, Concilio de Éfeso (Alejandría)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cirilo_de_Alejandr%C3%ADa" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.9]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"That was the true Light. The Divine Evangelist again profitably recapitulates what has been said, and clearly marks off That Which is in truth the Light, the Only-Begotten, from those that are not so, namely things originate: he severs clearly That Which is by nature from them which are by grace, That Which is partaken of from those which are participate of it"</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres distinguen claramente entre Cristo como Luz verdadera e increada, y las criaturas como luces participadas. Solo Cristo es Luz por naturaleza, mientras que otros son iluminados por Él.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('ptbf044ae2').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>La divinidad de Cristo demostrada por ser Luz verdadera</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="ptbf044ae2" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.9]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Where now are those who deny that He is true God? for here He is called 'the true Light' (c. xiv. 6), and elsewhere very 'Truth' and very 'Life.'"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Clement of Alexandria</strong> (c.150-215) <span class="patr-meta">— Maestro catequético, discípulo de Panteno (Alejandría)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clemente_de_Alejandr%C3%ADa" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.9]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Moses, then, was a sage, king, legislator. But our Saviour surpasses all human nature. He is so lovely, as to be alone loved by us, whose hearts are set on the true beauty, for 'He was the true light.' He is shown to be a King, as such hailed by unsophisticated children and by the unbelieving and ignorant Jews, and heralded by the prophets."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Pseudo-Athanasius</strong> (s.IV-V) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.8]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"It follows that the Word is the Son. But if the Son is the Light that has come into the world, beyond all dispute the world was made by the Son. For in the beginning of the Gospel, the Evangelist, speaking of John the Baptist, says, 'He was not that Light, but that he might bear witness concerning that Light.' For Christ himself was, as we have said before, the true Light that enlightens everyone that comes into the world."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres usan el título de 'Luz verdadera' como prueba de la divinidad de Cristo. Argumentan que solo Dios puede ser la fuente de toda iluminación espiritual.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="verse-block" id="vb9"><div class="verse-header"><span class="vnum">9</span></div><div class="greek-line" id="greek-9">Ἦν τὸ φῶς τὸ ἀληθινὸν ὃ φωτίζει πάντα ἄνθρωπον ἐρχόμενον εἰς τὸν κόσμον</div><div class="uncial-line" id="uncial-9" style="display:none;font-family:'Noto Serif',serif;font-size:0.9rem;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#5d4037;background:#efebe9;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;overflow-wrap:break-word" title="Así se vería este versículo en un manuscrito uncial del siglo IV — todo mayúsculas, sin espacios (puntos medios añadidos como ayuda visual)">ΗΝ·ΤΟ·ΦΩΣ·ΤΟ·ΑΛΗΘΙΝΟΝ·Ο·ΦΩΤΙΖΕΙ·ΠΑΝΤΑ·ΑΝΘΡΩΠΟΝ·ΕΡΧΟΜΕΝΟΝ·ΕΙΣ·ΤΟΝ·ΚΟΣΜΟΝ<span style="display:block;font-size:0.65rem;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:0;opacity:0.7"><a href="https://www.codexsinaiticus.org/en/manuscript.aspx?book=33&chapter=1&verse=9" target="_blank" style="color:#5d4037">Ver en Codex Sinaiticus →</a></span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:0.3rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:0.3rem;align-items:center"><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="toggleRVR(9)">RVR60</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('uncial-9').style.display=document.getElementById('uncial-9').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#efebe9;color:#5d4037;border-color:#bcaaa4" title="Escritura uncial: así se veía el NT en los manuscritos del s.IV (Vaticanus, Sinaiticus). Todo mayúsculas, sin espacios entre palabras (scriptio continua), sin acentos ni puntuación. La iota subscrita se escribe explícitamente.">Uncial</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('pron-9').style.display=document.getElementById('pron-9').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0;border-color:#90caf9" title="Pronunciación bizantina aproximada (griego moderno/eclesiástico)">Pronunciación</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-patr" onclick="toggleSection('patr-9')" title="32 citas patrísticas disponibles">✝ 32 patrística</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-exeg" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-9')" title="3 comentarios exegéticos">📚 3 exégesis</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-ver" onclick="document.getElementById('vers-9').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="9 versiones disponibles">📖 versiones</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('xrefs-9').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="8 referencias cruzadas">🔗 8 refs</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="copyVerse(9)" title="Copiar versículo al portapapeles" style="background:#f3e5f5;border-color:#ce93d8;color:#6a1b9a">📋</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('notes-9').style.display=document.getElementById('notes-9').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" title="Notas personales" style="background:#fff8e1;border-color:#ffd54f;color:#f57f17">📝</div></div><div id="rvr-9" class="collapsed spanish-line">Aquella luz verdadera, que alumbra a todo hombre, venía a este mundo.</div><div id="vers-9" class="collapsed" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR60</span>Aquella luz verdadera, que alumbra a todo hombre, venía a este mundo.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR1909</span>Aquel era la luz verdadera, que alumbra á todo hombre que viene á este mundo.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">KJV</span>That was the true Light, which lighteth every man that cometh into the world.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">ASV</span>There was the true light, even the light which lighteth every man, coming into the world. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">BSB</span>The true Light who gives light to every man was coming into the world. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Darby</span>The true light was that which, coming into the world, lightens every man. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">LITV</span>He was the true Light; He enlightens every man coming into the world. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">YLT</span>He was the true Light, which doth enlighten every man, coming to the world;</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Vulgate</span>erat lux vera quae inluminat omnem hominem venientem in mundum</div></div><div id="xrefs-9" class="collapsed xref-container" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 John 2:8" data-es="Otra vez os escribo un mandamiento nuevo, que es verdadero en él y en vosotros; porque las tinieblas son pasadas, y la verdadera luz ya alumbra." data-gr="πάλιν ἐντολὴν καινὴν γράφω ὑμῖν, ὅ ἐστιν ἀληθὲς ἐν αὐτῷ καὶ ἐν ὑμῖν, ὅτι ἡ σκοτία παράγεται καὶ τὸ φῶς τὸ ἀληθινὸν ἤδη φαίνει." data-lxx="" title="Otra vez os escribo un mandamiento nuevo, que es verdadero en él y en vosotros; …">1 John 2:8</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 John 5:20" data-es="Empero sabemos que el Hijo de Dios es venido, y nos ha dado entendimiento para conocer al que es verdadero: y estamos en el verdadero, en su Hijo Jesucristo. Este es el verdadero Dios, y la vida eterna." data-gr="οἴδαμεν δὲ ὅτι ὁ υἱὸς τοῦ θεοῦ ἥκει, καὶ δέδωκεν ἡμῖν διάνοιαν ἵνα ⸀γινώσκωμεν τὸν ἀληθινόν· καὶ ἐσμὲν ἐν τῷ ἀληθινῷ, ἐν τῷ υἱῷ αὐτοῦ Ἰησοῦ Χριστῷ. οὗτός ἐστιν ὁ ἀληθινὸς θεὸς καὶ ζωὴ αἰώνιος." data-lxx="" title="Empero sabemos que el Hijo de Dios es venido, y nos ha dado entendimiento para c…">1 John 5:20</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 Thessalonians 5:4" data-es="Mas vosotros, hermanos, no estáis en tinieblas, para que aquel día os sobrecoja como ladrón;" data-gr="ὑμεῖς δέ, ἀδελφοί, οὐκ ἐστὲ ἐν σκότει, ἵνα ἡ ἡμέρα ὑμᾶς ὡς ⸀κλέπτης καταλάβῃ," data-lxx="" title="Mas vosotros, hermanos, no estáis en tinieblas, para que aquel día os sobrecoja …">1 Thessalonians 5:4</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 Thessalonians 5:7" data-es="Porque los que duermen, de noche duermen; y los que están borrachos, de noche están borrachos." data-gr="οἱ γὰρ καθεύδοντες νυκτὸς καθεύδουσιν, καὶ οἱ μεθυσκόμενοι νυκτὸς μεθύουσιν·" data-lxx="" title="Porque los que duermen, de noche duermen; y los que están borrachos, de noche es…">1 Thessalonians 5:7</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Isaiah 49:6" data-es="Y dijo: Poco es que tú me seas siervo para levantar las tribus de Jacob, y para que restaures los asolamientos de Israel: también te dí por luz de las gentes, para que seas mi salud hasta lo postrero de la tierra." data-gr="וַ/יֹּ֗אמֶר נָקֵ֨ל מִֽ/הְיוֹתְ/ךָ֥ לִ/י֙ עֶ֔בֶד לְ/הָקִים֙ אֶת שִׁבְטֵ֣י יַעֲקֹ֔ב ו/נצירי וּ/נְצוּרֵ֥י יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל לְ/הָשִׁ֑יב וּ/נְתַתִּ֨י/ךָ֙ לְ/א֣וֹר גּוֹיִ֔ם לִֽ/הְי֥וֹת יְשׁוּעָתִ֖/י עַד קְצֵ֥ה הָ/אָֽרֶץ" data-lxx="καὶ εἶπέν μοι μέγα σοί ἐστιν τοῦ κληθῆναί σε παῖδά μου τοῦ στῆσαι τὰς φυλὰς Ιακωβ καὶ τὴν διασπορὰν τοῦ Ισραηλ ἐπιστρέψαι ἰδοὺ τέθεικά σε εἰς διαθήκην γένους εἰς φῶς ἐθνῶν τοῦ εἶναί σε εἰς σωτηρίαν ἕως ἐσχάτου τῆς γῆς" title="Y dijo: Poco es que tú me seas siervo para levantar las tribus de Jacob, y para …">Isaiah 49:6</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="John 12:46" data-es="Yo la luz he venido al mundo, para que todo aquel que cree en mí no permanezca en tinieblas." data-gr="ἐγὼ φῶς εἰς τὸν κόσμον ἐλήλυθα, ἵνα πᾶς ὁ πιστεύων εἰς ἐμὲ ἐν τῇ σκοτίᾳ μὴ μείνῃ." data-lxx="" title="Yo la luz he venido al mundo, para que todo aquel que cree en mí no permanezca e…">John 12:46</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="John 1:4" data-es="En él estaba la vida, y la vida era la luz de los hombres." data-gr="ἐν αὐτῷ ζωὴ ἦν, καὶ ἡ ζωὴ ἦν τὸ φῶς τῶν ἀνθρώπων·" data-lxx="" title="En él estaba la vida, y la vida era la luz de los hombres.">John 1:4</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="John 1:7" data-es="Este vino por testimonio, para que diese testimonio de la luz, para que todos creyesen por él." data-gr="οὗτος ἦλθεν εἰς μαρτυρίαν, ἵνα μαρτυρήσῃ περὶ τοῦ φωτός, ἵνα πάντες πιστεύσωσιν δι’ αὐτοῦ." data-lxx="" title="Este vino por testimonio, para que diese testimonio de la luz, para que todos cr…">John 1:7</span></div><div id="pron-9" style="display:none;font-size:0.85rem;color:#1565c0;background:#e3f2fd;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;font-style:italic" class="pron-line"></div><div id="notes-9" style="display:none;margin-bottom:0.5rem"><textarea id="note-input-9" style="width:100%;min-height:50px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;padding:4px 8px;font-size:0.82rem;resize:vertical" placeholder="Tus notas para v.9..." oninput="saveNote(9)"></textarea></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-9')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="exeg-9" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">📜</span> Exégesis del Griego <span class="arrow" id="arrow-exeg-9">▶</span></div><div id="exeg-9" class="collapsed section-content exeg-section" role="region"><div class="exeg-summary"><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Alford:</strong> to be taken with ἄνθρωπον (as lat [13] syrr cop [14] Orig [Exodus 2:0]; [Exodus 2:0] Epiph Chr Cyr Thl Euthym and most of the ancient Commentators and E.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Bengel:</strong> πάντα , every one ) every one, and wholly, so far as a man doth not withdraw himself from His influence: whosoever is enlightened at all, is enlightened by this Light.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Robertson:</strong> Emphatic position at the beginning of the sentence and so probably not periphrastic conjugation with ερχομενον (coming) near the end, though that is possible.<br></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv9_0').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Alford's Greek Testament</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1863)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv9_0" class="collapsed comm-body">9. ] The word ἀληθινόν (see reff.) in this connexion imports original, &lsquo;archetypal,&rsquo; and is used of the true genuine sources and patterns of those things which we find here below only in fragmentary imitations and derivations. Such an original was the Light here spoken of; but John was only a derived light, not lumen illuminans , but lumen illuminatum . The construction of this verse has been much disputed. Is ἐρχόμενον εἰς τ . κ . to be taken with ἄνθρωπον (as lat [13] syrr cop [14] Orig [Exodus 2:0]; [Exodus 2:0] Epiph Chr Cyr Thl Euthym and most of the ancient Commentators and E. V.), or does it belong to τὸ φῶς τὸ ἀλ . ? [13] The Latin versions: an abbreviated way of writing &lsquo;vulg lat- a b c &rsquo; &c. [14] The Coptic or Memphitic Egyptian version. Fourth century? The former construction can only be defended by a Rabbinical usage, by which כָּל בָּאֵי עוֹלָם means &lsquo;all men&rsquo; (Schöttgen, i. 223). But it is very questionable whether John ever speaks thus. Certainly he does not, in any of the passages commonly cited to defend this rendering, ch. [John 18:37] (which is spoken by Christ of Himself and His Mission); [John 16:21] ; [John 16:28] ; [John 12:46] . And even if he had thus spoken, how harsh and how unmeaning is the sentence; whether with Euthym [15] we lay an emphasis on ἦν , or with E. V. &c. supply τοῦτο before it. If this latter had been intended, surely it would have been more distinctly expressed; and even when it is supplied, we have in this verse only a less forcible repetition of [John 1:4] . [15] Euthymius Zigabenus, 1116 It seems then that we must join ἐρχ . εἰς τ . κ . with τ . φῶς τ . ἀληθ . But even then, three ways of rendering are apparently open to us. The first of these, which is that of Socinus, takes ἐρχόμ . κ . τ . λ . as meaning, &lsquo; at its coming into the world .&rsquo; This however besides the sense being inconsistent with Joh 1:4 leaves the opening clause without a demonstrative pronoun, as before. Then, secondly, ἐρχόμενον might seem to be used in the sense in which we frequently have ἐρχόμενος , as a quasi-future, &lsquo;who was, or is, to come:&rsquo; see [Matthew 11:3] ; Mar 10:30 alli [16] . fr.: ch. [John 6:14] ; [John 11:27] , in which last two places it is joined, as here, with εἰς τὸν κόσμον . But if this be adopted (which even constructionally is very doubtful), the only sense will be that the true light, &c. was to come; i.e. had not yet come; which manifestly is not correct; for it had come , when John gave his witness; and the whole of these Joh 1:6-13 relate to the time when He had appeared , and come to His own. [16] alli = some cursive mss. We are driven then to the only legitimate rendering, which is to take ἦν ἐρχόμενον as equivalent to an imperfect came: this usage being frequent in the N.T., see reff.: i.e. at the time when John bore this witness, the true light which lighteth every man, came was in process of manifesting Himself, into the world. Tholuck object</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv9_1').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Bengel's Gnomon</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1742)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv9_1" class="collapsed comm-body">[John 1:9] . Ἦν , was ) The Light itself, moreover, was that true light, which enlighteneth . The Effect shows the Subject, to whom the name of Light is most applicable [whose attributes entitle Him best to the name.] τὸ ἀληθινόν , the true ) There follows immediately the declaration, which enlighteneth , etc. This forms an antithesis to John, [who was only] a lamp, a witness. Comp. concerning the Truth , [John 1:14] ; [John 1:17] . ὃ φωτίζει , which enlighteneth ) It is proved by the effect, that this is the true light. It enlightens , the Present, in relation to the time, in which He came , as opposed to the former time, [John 1:5] . πάντα , every one ) every one, and wholly, so far as a man doth not withdraw himself from His influence: whosoever is enlightened at all, is enlightened by this Light. The singular number here has great force. Comp. [Colossians 1:28] [Warning every man and teaching every man, and that we may present every man perfect in Christ Jesus] [Romans 3:4] [Let God be true, but every man a liar]. Not even one is excluded. ἄνθρωπον , man ) Who by himself [when left to himself] is in darkness: every man has a more august sound, than all men , [John 1:7] . John was but a man , [John 1:6] . The Light, so far as it is light, is contradistinguished from man. ἐρχόμενον εἰς τὸν κόσμον , coming into the world ) ἐρχόμενον , coming is nominative, and depends on ἦν , was . A striking antithesis is thus presented: [ ἐγενέτο ] was made , [ ἀπεσταλμένος ] sent , [John 1:6] , and [ ἦν ] was , [ ἐρχόμενον ] coming [in this verse]: in which last word the Participle present, as often, has the force of an imperfect. Comp. ὤν , ch. [John 9:25] [ τυφλὸς ὢν , ἄρτι βλέπω , whereas I was blind, now I see] Notes: and elsewhere. Among the Hebrews it is a frequent periphrasis for a man. הבא בעולם , coming [a comer] into the world: but in the New Testament, and especially in this book, this phrase is used of Christ alone, and in an exalted sense. For He was, even before that He came. Thus evidently the phrase is applied ch. [John 3:19] , Light is come into the world: ch. [John 12:46] , I am come a light into the world. Presently after this [John 1:9] , succeeds the mention of the world and of His coming, repeated, [John 1:10-11] . The Son is also said to be sent by the Father, but not in the same way, as John is said to have been sent. Moreover the Son came, being sent and given, [Matthew 21:37] &ldquo;Last of all He sent unto them His Son;&rdquo; [John 3:16] , &ldquo;God so loved the world, that He gave His only begotten Son;&rdquo; ch. [John 11:27] , Martha, &ldquo;Thou art the Christ, the Son of God, which should come into the world;&rdquo; [Romans 8:3] ; [Romans 8:32] , &ldquo;God sending His own Son, in the likeness of sinful flesh He that spared not His own Son, but delivered Him up for us all;&rdquo; [1 John 3:8] , &ldquo;For this purpose the Son of God was manifested;&rdquo; [John 4:9] , &ldquo;God sent His only begotten Son into the world, that</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv9_2').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Robertson's Word Pictures</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1933)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv9_2" class="collapsed comm-body">There was ( ην ). Imperfect indicative. Emphatic position at the beginning of the sentence and so probably not periphrastic conjugation with ερχομενον (coming) near the end, though that is possible. The true light ( το φως το αληθινον ). "The light the genuine," not a false light of wreckers of ships, but the dependable light that guides to the harbor of safety. This true light had been on hand all the time in the darkness ( ην imperfect, linear action) before John came. Even the light (not in the Greek). Added in the English to make plain this interpretation. Lighteth every man ( φωτιζε παντα ανθρωπον ). Old verb (from φως ) to give light as in [Revelation 22:5]; [Luke 11:35]. The Quakers appeal to this phrase for their belief that to every man there is given an inner light that is a sufficient guide, the Quaker's text it is called. But it may only mean that all the real light that men receive comes from Christ, not necessarily that each one receives a special revelation. Coming ( ερχομενον ). This present middle participle of ερχομα can be taken with ανθρωπον just before (accusative masculine singular), "every man as he comes into the world." It can also be construed with φως (nominative neuter singular). This idea occurs in [John 3:19]; [John 11:27]; [John 12:46]. In the two last passages the phrase is used of the Messiah which makes it probable here. But even so the light presented in [John 11:27]; [John 12:46] is that of the Incarnate Messiah, not the Pre-incarnate Logos. Here κοσμος rather than παντα occurs in the sense of the orderly universe as often in this Gospel. See [Ephesians 1:4].</div></div><div class="themes-divider">🔍 Temas discutidos</div><div class="theme-card"><div class="theme-word">ἐρχόμενον εἰς τὸν κόσμον</div><div class="consensus-bar"><div style="width:25%;background:#f44336"></div></div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#4caf50">✅ <strong>Alford</strong> La construcción ha sido muy disputada: ¿se toma ἐρχόμενον con ἄνθρωπον o pertenece a τὸ φῶς τὸ ἀληθινόν?</div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#4caf50">✅ <strong>Bengel</strong> No aborda directamente la disputa construccional, enfocándose en el significado teológico.</div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#ff9800">⚠️ <strong>Robertson</strong> Posición enfática al comienzo sugiere que probablemente no es conjugación perifrástica con ἐρχόμενον.</div><div class="theme-summary">Existe desacuerdo significativo sobre si ἐρχόμενον modifica 'luz' o 'hombre', con Alford reconociendo la disputa y Robertson ofreciendo análisis gramatical.</div></div></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('patr-9')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="patr-9" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">👨‍🏫</span> Patrística · 4 temas · 32 citas <span class="arrow" id="arrow-patr-9">▶</span></div><div id="patr-9" class="collapsed section-content patr-section" role="region"><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt7e95915d').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Distinción entre luz creada y Luz increada</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt7e95915d" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.8]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Wherefore then did he come? 'But that he might bear witness concerning the light.' Why so? 'That all might believe through him.' And concerning what light was he to bear witness? 'That was the true light.' Wherefore is it added true? Because an enlightened man is also called a light; but the true light is that which enlightens. For even our eyes are called lights; and nevertheless, unless either during the night a lamp is lighted, or during the day the sun goes forth, these lights are open in vain."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.8]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"John, a man of distinguished grace, was sent before Him, a man enlightened by Him who is the Light. For of John it is said, 'He was not the Light, but that he should bear witness of the Light.' He may himself be called a light indeed, and rightly so; but an enlightened, not an enlightening light. The light that enlightens, and that which is enlightened, are different things: for even our eyes are called lights, and yet when we open them in the dark, they do not see."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> (c.376-444) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Alejandría, Concilio de Éfeso (Alejandría)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cirilo_de_Alejandr%C3%ADa" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.9]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"That was the true Light. The Divine Evangelist again profitably recapitulates what has been said, and clearly marks off That Which is in truth the Light, the Only-Begotten, from those that are not so, namely things originate: he severs clearly That Which is by nature from them which are by grace, That Which is partaken of from those which are participate of it"</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres distinguen claramente entre Cristo como Luz verdadera e increada, y las criaturas como luces participadas. Solo Cristo es Luz por naturaleza, mientras que otros son iluminados por Él.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt5d5ea9f4').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Cristo como Luz verdadera que ilumina a todo hombre</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt5d5ea9f4" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.9]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"But where is that light? 'He was the true light, which lighteth every man that cometh into the world.' If every man that cometh, then also John. The true light, therefore, enlightened him by whom He desired Himself to be pointed out. Understand, beloved, for He came to infirm minds, to wounded hearts, to the gaze of dim-eyed souls."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#ff9800"><div class="patr-cite-header">⚠️ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.9]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"If He 'lighteth every man that cometh into the world,' how is it that so many continue unenlightened? for not all have known the majesty of Christ. How then doth He 'light every man'? He lighteth all as far as in Him lies. But if some, wilfully closing the eyes of their mind, would not receive the rays of that Light, their darkness arises not from the nature of the Light, but from their own wickedness, who willfully deprive themselves of the gift."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> (c.376-444) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Alejandría, Concilio de Éfeso (Alejandría)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cirilo_de_Alejandr%C3%ADa" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.9]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"The rational portion of the creation, being enlightened, enlightens by sharing ideas from one mind as they are poured into another. Such enlightenment will rightly be called teaching rather than revelation. But the Word of God 'enlightens everyone that comes into the world,' not after the manner of teaching, as the angels, for example, or people, but rather, as God after the mode of creation, he engrafts in each of those that are called into being the seed of wisdom or of divine knowledge"</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres afirman que Cristo ilumina a todo hombre, pero debaten si esto es universal efectivo o potencial. Algunos explican que la falta de iluminación se debe al rechazo humano, no a deficiencia de la Luz.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt0acd7357').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>La eternidad y preexistencia de Cristo como Luz</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt0acd7357" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.9]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"That was the true Light, which lighteth every man that cometh into the world. For since above in speaking of John he said, that he came 'to bear witness of that Light'; and that he was sent in these our days; lest any one at hearing this should, on account of the recent coming of the witness, conceive some like suspicion concerning Him, who is witnessed of, he has carried up the imagination, and transported it to that existence which is before all beginning, which has neither end nor commencement"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.9]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Let us not then remove the eternal bounds which our fathers set, but let us ever yield to the laws of the Spirit; and when we hear that 'That was the true Light,' let us seek to discover nothing more. For it is not possible to pass beyond this saying. Had His generation been like that of a man, needs must there have been an interval between the begetter and the begotten; but since it is in a manner ineffable and becoming God, give up the 'before' and the 'after,' for these are the names of points of time"</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres enfatizan que Cristo como Luz verdadera es eterno y preexistente, sin comienzo ni fin. Su existencia trasciende el tiempo y las categorías humanas de generación.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt1bfa4b14').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>La divinidad de Cristo demostrada por ser Luz verdadera</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt1bfa4b14" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.9]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Where now are those who deny that He is true God? for here He is called 'the true Light' (c. xiv. 6), and elsewhere very 'Truth' and very 'Life.'"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Clement of Alexandria</strong> (c.150-215) <span class="patr-meta">— Maestro catequético, discípulo de Panteno (Alejandría)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clemente_de_Alejandr%C3%ADa" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.9]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Moses, then, was a sage, king, legislator. But our Saviour surpasses all human nature. He is so lovely, as to be alone loved by us, whose hearts are set on the true beauty, for 'He was the true light.' He is shown to be a King, as such hailed by unsophisticated children and by the unbelieving and ignorant Jews, and heralded by the prophets."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Pseudo-Athanasius</strong> (s.IV-V) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.8]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"It follows that the Word is the Son. But if the Son is the Light that has come into the world, beyond all dispute the world was made by the Son. For in the beginning of the Gospel, the Evangelist, speaking of John the Baptist, says, 'He was not that Light, but that he might bear witness concerning that Light.' For Christ himself was, as we have said before, the true Light that enlightens everyone that comes into the world."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres usan el título de 'Luz verdadera' como prueba de la divinidad de Cristo. Argumentan que solo Dios puede ser la fuente de toda iluminación espiritual.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="verse-block" id="vb10"><div class="verse-header"><span class="vnum">10</span></div><div class="greek-line" id="greek-10">ἐν τῷ κόσμῳ ἦν καὶ ὁ κόσμος δι᾽ αὐτοῦ ἐγένετο καὶ ὁ κόσμος αὐτὸν οὐκ ἔγνω</div><div class="uncial-line" id="uncial-10" style="display:none;font-family:'Noto Serif',serif;font-size:0.9rem;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#5d4037;background:#efebe9;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;overflow-wrap:break-word" title="Así se vería este versículo en un manuscrito uncial del siglo IV — todo mayúsculas, sin espacios (puntos medios añadidos como ayuda visual)">ΕΝ·ΤΩΙ·ΚΟΣΜΩΙ·ΗΝ·ΚΑΙ·Ο·ΚΟΣΜΟΣ·ΔΙ·ΑΥΤΟΥ·ΕΓΕΝΕΤΟ·ΚΑΙ·Ο·ΚΟΣΜΟΣ·ΑΥΤΟΝ·ΟΥΚ·ΕΓΝΩ<span style="display:block;font-size:0.65rem;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:0;opacity:0.7"><a href="https://www.codexsinaiticus.org/en/manuscript.aspx?book=33&chapter=1&verse=10" target="_blank" style="color:#5d4037">Ver en Codex Sinaiticus →</a></span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:0.3rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:0.3rem;align-items:center"><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="toggleRVR(10)">RVR60</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('uncial-10').style.display=document.getElementById('uncial-10').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#efebe9;color:#5d4037;border-color:#bcaaa4" title="Escritura uncial: así se veía el NT en los manuscritos del s.IV (Vaticanus, Sinaiticus). Todo mayúsculas, sin espacios entre palabras (scriptio continua), sin acentos ni puntuación. La iota subscrita se escribe explícitamente.">Uncial</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('pron-10').style.display=document.getElementById('pron-10').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0;border-color:#90caf9" title="Pronunciación bizantina aproximada (griego moderno/eclesiástico)">Pronunciación</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-patr" onclick="toggleSection('patr-10')" title="23 citas patrísticas disponibles">✝ 23 patrística</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-exeg" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-10')" title="3 comentarios exegéticos">📚 3 exégesis</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-ver" onclick="document.getElementById('vers-10').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="9 versiones disponibles">📖 versiones</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('xrefs-10').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="8 referencias cruzadas">🔗 8 refs</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="copyVerse(10)" title="Copiar versículo al portapapeles" style="background:#f3e5f5;border-color:#ce93d8;color:#6a1b9a">📋</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('notes-10').style.display=document.getElementById('notes-10').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" title="Notas personales" style="background:#fff8e1;border-color:#ffd54f;color:#f57f17">📝</div></div><div id="rvr-10" class="collapsed spanish-line">En el mundo estaba, y el mundo por él fue hecho; pero el mundo no le conoció.</div><div id="vers-10" class="collapsed" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR60</span>En el mundo estaba, y el mundo por él fue hecho; pero el mundo no le conoció.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR1909</span>En el mundo estaba, y el mundo fué hecho por él; y el mundo no le conoció.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">KJV</span>He was in the world, and the world was made by him, and the world knew him not.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">ASV</span>He was in the world, and the world was made through him, and the world knew him not. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">BSB</span>He was in the world, and though the world was made through Him, the world did not recognize Him. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Darby</span>He was in the world, and the world had [its] being through him, and the world knew him not. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">LITV</span>He was in the world, and the world came into being through Him, yet the world did not know Him. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">YLT</span>in the world he was, and the world through him was made, and the world did not know him:</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Vulgate</span>in mundo erat et mundus per ipsum factus est et mundus eum non cognovit</div></div><div id="xrefs-10" class="collapsed xref-container" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 Corinthians 1:21" data-es="Porque por no haber el mundo conocido en la sabiduría de Dios á Dios por sabiduría, agradó á Dios salvar á los creyentes por la locura de la predicación." data-gr="ἐπειδὴ γὰρ ἐν τῇ σοφίᾳ τοῦ θεοῦ οὐκ ἔγνω ὁ κόσμος διὰ τῆς σοφίας τὸν θεόν, εὐδόκησεν ὁ θεὸς διὰ τῆς μωρίας τοῦ κηρύγματος σῶσαι τοὺς πιστεύοντας." data-lxx="" title="Porque por no haber el mundo conocido en la sabiduría de Dios á Dios por sabidur…">1 Corinthians 1:21</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 Corinthians 2:8" data-es="La que ninguno de los príncipes de este siglo conoció; porque si la hubieran conocido, nunca hubieran crucificado al Señor de gloria:" data-gr="ἣν οὐδεὶς τῶν ἀρχόντων τοῦ αἰῶνος τούτου ἔγνωκεν, εἰ γὰρ ἔγνωσαν, οὐκ ἂν τὸν κύριον τῆς δόξης ἐσταύρωσαν·" data-lxx="" title="La que ninguno de los príncipes de este siglo conoció; porque si la hubieran con…">1 Corinthians 2:8</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 John 3:1" data-es="MIRAD cuál amor nos ha dado el Padre, que seamos llamados hijos de Dios: por esto el mundo no nos conoce, porque no le conoce á él." data-gr="ἴδετε ποταπὴν ἀγάπην δέδωκεν ἡμῖν ὁ πατὴρ ἵνα τέκνα θεοῦ κληθῶμεν, ⸂καὶ ἐσμέν⸃. διὰ τοῦτο ὁ κόσμος οὐ γινώσκει ⸀ἡμᾶς ὅτι οὐκ ἔγνω αὐτόν." data-lxx="" title="MIRAD cuál amor nos ha dado el Padre, que seamos llamados hijos de Dios: por est…">1 John 3:1</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Acts 17:24" data-es="El Dios que hizo el mundo y todas las cosas que en él hay, éste, como sea Señor del cielo y de la tierra, no habita en templos hechos de manos," data-gr="ὁ θεὸς ὁ ποιήσας τὸν κόσμον καὶ πάντα τὰ ἐν αὐτῷ, οὗτος οὐρανοῦ καὶ γῆς ⸂ὑπάρχων κύριος⸃ οὐκ ἐν χειροποιήτοις ναοῖς κατοικεῖ" data-lxx="" title="El Dios que hizo el mundo y todas las cosas que en él hay, éste, como sea Señor …">Acts 17:24</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Acts 17:27" data-es="Para que buscasen á Dios, si en alguna manera, palpando, le hallen; aunque cierto no está lejos de cada uno de nosotros:" data-gr="ζητεῖν τὸν ⸀θεὸν εἰ ἄρα γε ψηλαφήσειαν αὐτὸν καὶ εὕροιεν, καί γε οὐ μακρὰν ἀπὸ ἑνὸς ἑκάστου ἡμῶν ὑπάρχοντα." data-lxx="" title="Para que buscasen á Dios, si en alguna manera, palpando, le hallen; aunque ciert…">Acts 17:27</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Hebrews 11:3" data-es="Por la fe entendemos haber sido compuestos los siglos por la palabra de Dios, siendo hecho lo que se ve, de lo que no se veía." data-gr="πίστει νοοῦμεν κατηρτίσθαι τοὺς αἰῶνας ῥήματι θεοῦ, εἰς τὸ μὴ ἐκ φαινομένων ⸂τὸ βλεπόμενον⸃ γεγονέναι." data-lxx="" title="Por la fe entendemos haber sido compuestos los siglos por la palabra de Dios, si…">Hebrews 11:3</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="John 17:25" data-es="Padre justo, el mundo no te ha conocido, mas yo te he conocido; y éstos han conocido que tú me enviaste;" data-gr="⸀Πάτερ δίκαιε, καὶ ὁ κόσμος σε οὐκ ἔγνω, ἐγὼ δέ σε ἔγνων, καὶ οὗτοι ἔγνωσαν ὅτι σύ με ἀπέστειλας," data-lxx="" title="Padre justo, el mundo no te ha conocido, mas yo te he conocido; y éstos han cono…">John 17:25</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="John 1:18" data-es="A Dios nadie le vió jamás: el unigénito Hijo, que está en el seno del Padre, él le declaró." data-gr="θεὸν οὐδεὶς ἑώρακεν πώποτε· ⸂μονογενὴς θεὸς⸃ ὁ ὢν εἰς τὸν κόλπον τοῦ πατρὸς ἐκεῖνος ἐξηγήσατο." data-lxx="" title="A Dios nadie le vió jamás: el unigénito Hijo, que está en el seno del Padre, él …">John 1:18</span></div><div id="pron-10" style="display:none;font-size:0.85rem;color:#1565c0;background:#e3f2fd;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;font-style:italic" class="pron-line"></div><div id="notes-10" style="display:none;margin-bottom:0.5rem"><textarea id="note-input-10" style="width:100%;min-height:50px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;padding:4px 8px;font-size:0.82rem;resize:vertical" placeholder="Tus notas para v.10..." oninput="saveNote(10)"></textarea></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-10')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="exeg-10" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">📜</span> Exégesis del Griego <span class="arrow" id="arrow-exeg-10">▶</span></div><div id="exeg-10" class="collapsed section-content exeg-section" role="region"><div class="exeg-summary"><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Alford:</strong> ] The κόσμος is the created world, into which He came ( Joh 1:9 ), which was made by Him ( Joh 1:3 ), which nevertheless (i.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Bengel:</strong> &rdquo; But in that passage Ἡ ΣΥΝΤΈΛΕΙΑ ΤῶΝ ΑἸΏΝΩΝ does not mean the putting off of the end of the world on [subject to] a condition, but categorically denotes the last times of the world, as opposed …<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Robertson:</strong> Second aorist active indicative of common verb γινοσκω , what Gildersleeve called a negative aorist, refused or failed to recognize him, his world that he had created and that was held together by him…<br></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv10_0').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Alford's Greek Testament</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1863)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv10_0" class="collapsed comm-body">10. ] The κόσμος is the created world, into which He came ( Joh 1:9 ), which was made by Him ( Joh 1:3 ), which nevertheless (i.e. as here represented by man , the only creature who γινώσκει ) knew, recognized Him not. καί is as in [John 1:5] . αὐτόν , not αὐτό , because though τὸ φῶς has been the subject, yet the δι ʼ αὐτοῦ ἐγένετο brings in again the creative λόγος , Who is the Light. The three members of the sentence form a climax; He was in the world (and therefore the world should have known Him), and the world was made by Him (much more then should it have known Him), and the world knew Him not.</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv10_1').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Bengel's Gnomon</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1742)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv10_1" class="collapsed comm-body">[John 1:10] . Ἐν τῷ κόσμῷ ἦν , He was in the world ) The evangelist adds this, lest any one should so understand the expression, coming into the world , as if the Light had not been previously in the world at all. Three times in this verse world is repeated; three times it is said of the human race, as in the previous verse, but not to the exclusion of the other creatures, at least in the first place. δἰ αὐτοῦ ἐγένετο , was made by Him ) αὐτοῦ , masculine, as presently after αὐτόν . It is referred to the sense, [16] though Φῶς is neuter. Artemonius, p. 439, 450, etc., maintains that there is meant here the dissolution of all things, which was now about to have taken place, at the time when Christ suffered, had it not been turned aside [removed] by His own sacrifice, and for that purpose he quotes the passage, [Hebrews 9:26] , &ldquo;Now once in the end of the world hath He appeared to put away sin by the sacrifice of Himself.&rdquo; But in that passage Ἡ ΣΥΝΤΈΛΕΙΑ ΤῶΝ ΑἸΏΝΩΝ does not mean the putting off of the end of the world on [subject to] a condition, but categorically denotes the last times of the world, as opposed to the many ages that have elapsed since the foundation of the world. If such an interpretation [as Artemonius&rsquo;] holds good, Israel too might be said to be made by Moses ; inasmuch as he averted its dissolution. With the same purpose in view, Artemonius, p. 455, urges the order of time in the clauses of this verse, but without reason. There is rather in it a gradation, wherein the world is urged to the acknowledgment of the Light by that [first] reason He was in the world , but more so by this [second reason] and the world was made by Him ; or in other words, began to be . καὶ , and ) and yet. ὁ κόσμος , the world ) The name world in the sacred writings implies THE IMPIOUS SILLINESS [futilitatem, emptiness] OF THE HUMAN RACE. Camer. note in [John 17:0] . [16] By the figure πρὸς τὸ σημαινόμενον . E. and T.</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv10_2').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Robertson's Word Pictures</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1933)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv10_2" class="collapsed comm-body">He was in the world ( εν τω κοσμω ην ). Imperfect tense of continuous existence in the universe before the Incarnation as in verses [John 1:1]; [John 1:2]. Was made by him ( δι' αυτου εγενετο ). "Through him." Same statement here of "the world" ( ο κοσμος ) as that made in verse [John 1:3] of παντα . Knew him not ( αυτον ουκ εγνω ). Second aorist active indicative of common verb γινοσκω , what Gildersleeve called a negative aorist, refused or failed to recognize him, his world that he had created and that was held together by him ([Colossians 1:16]). Not only did the world fail to know the Pre-incarnate Logos, but it failed to recognize him when he became Incarnate ([John 1:26]). Two examples in this sentence of John's fondness for κα as in verses [John 1:1]; [John 1:4]; [John 1:5]; [John 1:14], the paratactic rather than the hypotactic construction, like the common Hebrew use of wav.</div></div></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('patr-10')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="patr-10" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">👨‍🏫</span> Patrística · 5 temas · 23 citas <span class="arrow" id="arrow-patr-10">▶</span></div><div id="patr-10" class="collapsed section-content patr-section" role="region"><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('ptc916f310').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Creación del mundo por el Verbo</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="ptc916f310" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Irenaeus</strong> (c.130-202) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Lyon, mártir, discípulo de Policarpo (discípulo de Juan) (Lyon)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ireneo_de_Lyon" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.10]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"John, however, does himself put this matter beyond all controversy on our part, when he says, 'He was in this world, and the world was made by Him, and the world knew Him not. He came unto His own [things], and His own [people] received Him not.' But according to Marcion, and those like him, neither was the world made by Him; nor did He come to His own things, but to those of another. And, according to certain of the Gnostics, this world was made by angels, and not by the Word of God."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> (c.376-444) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Alejandría, Concilio de Éfeso (Alejandría)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cirilo_de_Alejandr%C3%ADa" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.10]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"The Evangelist in these words needfully indicates that the world was made through the Very Light, that is, the Only-Begotten. For although, having called Him most distinctly Word at the beginning, he affirmed that all things were made through Him, and that without Him nothing was brought into being, and demonstrated thereby that He was their Maker and Creator: yet it was necessary now most particularly to take this up again anew, that no room of error and perdition"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.10]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"But not as of equal duration with the world. Away with the thought. Wherefore he adds, 'And the world was made by Him'; thus leading thee up again to the eternal existence of the Only-Begotten. For he who has heard that this universe is His work, though he be very dull, though he be a hater, though he be an enemy of the glory of God, will certainly, willing or unwilling, be forced to confess that the maker is before his works."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres afirman unánimemente que el mundo fue creado por el Verbo, usando este versículo contra gnósticos y marcionitas que negaban la creación divina. La creación demuestra la eternidad del Hijo como anterior a sus obras.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt2de1dde9').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Presencia divina del Verbo en el mundo</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt2de1dde9" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.10]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"He is said to have come to us, not by traveling through space but by appearing to mortals in human flesh. He came, then, to that place where he already was, because he was in the world and the world was made by him."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.10]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"What then? If He came hither, where was He? 'He was in this world.' He was both here and came hither; He was here according to His divinity, and He came hither according to the flesh; because when He was here according to His divinity, He could not be seen by the foolish, by the blind, and the wicked."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> (c.376-444) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Alejandría, Concilio de Éfeso (Alejandría)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cirilo_de_Alejandr%C3%ADa" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.10]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"What does he say next? That He was in the world. Profitably does the Divine add this also, introducing thereby a thought most needful for us. For when he said, He was the Very Light which lighteth every man coming into the world, and it was not wholly clear to the hearers, whether it meant that the Light lighteth every man that cometh into the world, or that the Very Light itself, passing as from some other place into the world, maketh its illumination of all men"</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres enseñan que el Verbo estaba presente en el mundo por su divinidad antes de la Encarnación, y vino en la carne al lugar donde ya estaba espiritualmente. Su presencia divina es omnipresente y eterna.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt8435ec6e').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Ignorancia del mundo hacia su Creador</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt8435ec6e" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.10]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Which world was made through him that did not know him? I mean, it wasn't the world that was through him that did not know him. What is the world that was made through him? Heaven and earth. How can it be that the heavens did not know him, when during his passion the sun was darkened? How that the earth did not know him, seeing that it quaked as he hung there? But 'the world did not know him,' the world whose prince is the one of whom it is said, 'Behold, the prince of this world is coming'"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.10]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"By 'the world' he here means the multitude, which is corrupt, and closely attached to earthly things, the common turbulent, silly people. For the friends and favorites of God all knew Him, even before His coming in the flesh."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.10]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"But, because of their eagerness to enjoy the creature in place of the Creator, people have been conformed to this world and have been fittingly called 'the world.' Consequently, they did not know wisdom, and, therefore, the Evangelist said, 'the world knew him not.'"</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres distinguen entre el mundo físico que reconoció a Cristo (sol oscurecido, tierra tembló) y el mundo moral de los hombres pecadores que lo rechazaron. La ignorancia se debe al apego a las criaturas en lugar del Creador.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt330f7005').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Encarnación como manifestación visible</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt330f7005" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.10]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"The Light which lighteneth every man that cometh into the world, came here in the flesh; because while He was here in His Divinity alone, the foolish, blind, and un-righteous could not discern Him; those of whom it is said above, The darkness comprehended it not. Hence the text; He was in the world."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Chrysostom</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.10]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"as in the world, and the world was made by Him' (John i. 10 ): how is He 'brought in,' otherwise than in the flesh?"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>1 Clement</strong> (s.I-II) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Roma, discípulo de Pedro y Pablo (Roma)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clemente_de_Roma" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.11]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"For the Creator of the world is truly the Word of God: and this is our Lord, who in the last times was made man, existing in this world, and who in an invisible manner contains all things created, and is inherent in the entire creation, since the Word of God governs and arranges all things; and therefore He came to His own in a visible manner, and was made flesh, and hung upon the tree, that He might sum up all things in Himself."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres enseñan que la Encarnación fue necesaria para hacer visible al Verbo invisible, permitiendo que los hombres ciegos espiritualmente pudieran percibirlo. La carne fue el medio de manifestación divina al mundo.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt7c8f7d5c').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Propósito soteriológico de la venida de Cristo</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt7c8f7d5c" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Maximus the Confessor</strong> (c.580-662) <span class="patr-meta">— Monje teólogo, mártir (mutilado) (Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/M%C3%A1ximo_el_Confesor" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.10]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"[The incarnation of the Logos] is the blessed end on account of which everything was created. This is the divine purpose, which was thought of before the beginning of creation and which we call an intended fulfillment. All creation exists on account of this fulfillment, and yet the fulfillment itself exists because of nothing that was created. Since God had this end in full view, he produced the natures of things."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Thomas Aquinas</strong> (1225-1274) <span class="patr-meta">— Teólogo escolástico, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Alberto Magno (Italia)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom%C3%A1s_de_Aquino" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.11]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Having given the necessity for the incarnation of the Word, the Evangelist then shows the advantage men gained from that incarnation. First, he shows the coming of the light (v 11); secondly, its reception by men (v 11b); thirdly, the fruit brought by the coming of the light (v 12)."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres ven la Encarnación como el propósito eterno de Dios, el fin para el cual fue creado todo. No fue una respuesta al pecado sino el plan divino original para la salvación y perfección de la creación.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="verse-block" id="vb11"><div class="verse-header"><span class="vnum">11</span></div><div class="greek-line" id="greek-11">εἰς τὰ ἴδια ἦλθεν καὶ οἱ ἴδιοι αὐτὸν οὐ παρέλαβον</div><div class="uncial-line" id="uncial-11" style="display:none;font-family:'Noto Serif',serif;font-size:0.9rem;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#5d4037;background:#efebe9;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;overflow-wrap:break-word" title="Así se vería este versículo en un manuscrito uncial del siglo IV — todo mayúsculas, sin espacios (puntos medios añadidos como ayuda visual)">ΕΙΣ·ΤΑ·ΙΔΙΑ·ΗΛΘΕΝ·ΚΑΙ·ΟΙ·ΙΔΙΟΙ·ΑΥΤΟΝ·ΟΥ·ΠΑΡΕΛΑΒΟΝ<span style="display:block;font-size:0.65rem;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:0;opacity:0.7"><a href="https://www.codexsinaiticus.org/en/manuscript.aspx?book=33&chapter=1&verse=11" target="_blank" style="color:#5d4037">Ver en Codex Sinaiticus →</a></span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:0.3rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:0.3rem;align-items:center"><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="toggleRVR(11)">RVR60</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('uncial-11').style.display=document.getElementById('uncial-11').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#efebe9;color:#5d4037;border-color:#bcaaa4" title="Escritura uncial: así se veía el NT en los manuscritos del s.IV (Vaticanus, Sinaiticus). Todo mayúsculas, sin espacios entre palabras (scriptio continua), sin acentos ni puntuación. La iota subscrita se escribe explícitamente.">Uncial</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('pron-11').style.display=document.getElementById('pron-11').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0;border-color:#90caf9" title="Pronunciación bizantina aproximada (griego moderno/eclesiástico)">Pronunciación</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-patr" onclick="toggleSection('patr-11')" title="106 citas patrísticas disponibles">✝ 106 patrística</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-exeg" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-11')" title="3 comentarios exegéticos">📚 3 exégesis</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-ver" onclick="document.getElementById('vers-11').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="9 versiones disponibles">📖 versiones</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('xrefs-11').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="8 referencias cruzadas">🔗 8 refs</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="copyVerse(11)" title="Copiar versículo al portapapeles" style="background:#f3e5f5;border-color:#ce93d8;color:#6a1b9a">📋</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('notes-11').style.display=document.getElementById('notes-11').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" title="Notas personales" style="background:#fff8e1;border-color:#ffd54f;color:#f57f17">📝</div></div><div id="rvr-11" class="collapsed spanish-line">A lo suyo vino, y los suyos no le recibieron.</div><div id="vers-11" class="collapsed" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR60</span>A lo suyo vino, y los suyos no le recibieron.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR1909</span>A lo suyo vino, y los suyos no le recibieron.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">KJV</span>He came unto his own, and his own received him not.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">ASV</span>He came unto his own, and they that were his own received him not. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">BSB</span>He came to His own, and His own did not receive Him. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Darby</span>He came to his own, and his own received him not; </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">LITV</span>He came to His own, and His own did not receive Him. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">YLT</span>to his own things he came, and his own people did not receive him;</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Vulgate</span>in propria venit et sui eum non receperunt</div></div><div id="xrefs-11" class="collapsed xref-container" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Acts 7:51" data-es="Duros de cerviz, é incircuncisos de corazón y de oídos, vosotros resistís siempre al Espíritu Santo: como vuestros padres, así también vosotros." data-gr="Σκληροτράχηλοι καὶ ἀπερίτμητοι ⸀καρδίαις καὶ τοῖς ὠσίν, ὑμεῖς ἀεὶ τῷ πνεύματι τῷ ἁγίῳ ἀντιπίπτετε, ὡς οἱ πατέρες ὑμῶν καὶ ὑμεῖς." data-lxx="" title="Duros de cerviz, é incircuncisos de corazón y de oídos, vosotros resistís siempr…">Acts 7:51</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Acts 7:52" data-es="¿A cuál de los profetas no persiguieron vuestros padres? y mataron á los que antes anunciaron la venida del Justo, del cual vosotros ahora habéis sido entregadores y matadores;" data-gr="τίνα τῶν προφητῶν οὐκ ἐδίωξαν οἱ πατέρες ὑμῶν; καὶ ἀπέκτειναν τοὺς προκαταγγείλαντας περὶ τῆς ἐλεύσεως τοῦ δικαίου οὗ νῦν ὑμεῖς προδόται καὶ φονεῖς ⸀ἐγένεσθε," data-lxx="" title="¿A cuál de los profetas no persiguieron vuestros padres? y mataron á los que ant…">Acts 7:52</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Isaiah 53:2" data-es="Y subirá cual renuevo delante de él, y como raíz de tierra seca: no hay parecer en él, ni hermosura: verlo hemos, mas sin atractivo para que le deseemos." data-gr="וַ/יַּ֨עַל כַּ/יּוֹנֵ֜ק לְ/פָנָ֗י/ו וְ/כַ/שֹּׁ֨רֶשׁ֙ מֵ/אֶ֣רֶץ צִיָּ֔ה לֹא תֹ֥אַר ל֖/וֹ וְ/לֹ֣א הָדָ֑ר וְ/נִרְאֵ֥/הוּ וְ/לֹֽא מַרְאֶ֖ה וְ/נֶחְמְדֵֽ/הוּ" data-lxx="ἀνηγγείλαμεν ἐναντίον αὐτοῦ ὡς παιδίον ὡς ῥίζα ἐν γῇ διψώσῃ οὐκ ἔστιν εἶδος αὐτῷ οὐδὲ δόξα καὶ εἴδομεν αὐτόν καὶ οὐκ εἶχεν εἶδος οὐδὲ κάλλος" title="Y subirá cual renuevo delante de él, y como raíz de tierra seca: no hay parecer …">Isaiah 53:2</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Isaiah 53:3" data-es="Despreciado y desechado entre los hombres, varón de dolores, experimentado en quebranto: y como que escondimos de él el rostro, fué menospreciado, y no lo estimamos." data-gr="נִבְזֶה֙ וַ/חֲדַ֣ל אִישִׁ֔ים אִ֥ישׁ מַכְאֹב֖וֹת וִ/יד֣וּעַ חֹ֑לִי וּ/כְ/מַסְתֵּ֤ר פָּנִים֙ מִמֶּ֔/נּוּ נִבְזֶ֖ה וְ/לֹ֥א חֲשַׁבְנֻֽ/הוּ" data-lxx="ἀλλὰ τὸ εἶδος αὐτοῦ ἄτιμον ἐκλεῖπον παρὰ πάντας ἀνθρώπους ἄνθρωπος ἐν πληγῇ ὢν καὶ εἰδὼς φέρειν μαλακίαν ὅτι ἀπέστραπται τὸ πρόσωπον αὐτοῦ ἠτιμάσθη καὶ οὐκ ἐλογίσθη" title="Despreciado y desechado entre los hombres, varón de dolores, experimentado en qu…">Isaiah 53:3</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="John 3:32" data-es="Y lo que vió y oyó, esto testifica: y nadie recibe su testimonio." data-gr="⸀ὃ ἑώρακεν καὶ ἤκουσεν τοῦτο μαρτυρεῖ, καὶ τὴν μαρτυρίαν αὐτοῦ οὐδεὶς λαμβάνει." data-lxx="" title="Y lo que vió y oyó, esto testifica: y nadie recibe su testimonio.">John 3:32</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Luke 19:14" data-es="Empero sus ciudadanos le aborrecían, y enviaron tras de él una embajada, diciendo: No queremos que éste reine sobre nosotros." data-gr="οἱ δὲ πολῖται αὐτοῦ ἐμίσουν αὐτόν, καὶ ἀπέστειλαν πρεσβείαν ὀπίσω αὐτοῦ λέγοντες· Οὐ θέλομεν τοῦτον βασιλεῦσαι ἐφ’ ἡμᾶς." data-lxx="" title="Empero sus ciudadanos le aborrecían, y enviaron tras de él una embajada, diciend…">Luke 19:14</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Luke 20:13" data-es="Entonces el señor de la viña dijo: ¿Qué haré? Enviaré mi hijo amado: quizás cuando á éste vieren, tendrán respeto." data-gr="εἶπεν δὲ ὁ κύριος τοῦ ἀμπελῶνος· Τί ποιήσω; πέμψω τὸν υἱόν μου τὸν ἀγαπητόν· ἴσως ⸀τοῦτον ἐντραπήσονται." data-lxx="" title="Entonces el señor de la viña dijo: ¿Qué haré? Enviaré mi hijo amado: quizás cuan…">Luke 20:13</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Luke 20:15" data-es="Y echáronle fuera de la viña, y le mataron. ¿Qué pues, les hará el señor de la viña?" data-gr="καὶ ἐκβαλόντες αὐτὸν ἔξω τοῦ ἀμπελῶνος ἀπέκτειναν. τί οὖν ποιήσει αὐτοῖς ὁ κύριος τοῦ ἀμπελῶνος;" data-lxx="" title="Y echáronle fuera de la viña, y le mataron. ¿Qué pues, les hará el señor de la v…">Luke 20:15</span></div><div id="pron-11" style="display:none;font-size:0.85rem;color:#1565c0;background:#e3f2fd;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;font-style:italic" class="pron-line"></div><div id="notes-11" style="display:none;margin-bottom:0.5rem"><textarea id="note-input-11" style="width:100%;min-height:50px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;padding:4px 8px;font-size:0.82rem;resize:vertical" placeholder="Tus notas para v.11..." oninput="saveNote(11)"></textarea></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-11')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="exeg-11" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">📜</span> Exégesis del Griego <span class="arrow" id="arrow-exeg-11">▶</span></div><div id="exeg-11" class="collapsed section-content exeg-section" role="region"><div class="exeg-summary"><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Alford:</strong> ] τὰ ἴδια here cannot well mean the world , or οἱ ἴδιοι mankind in general: it would be difficult to point out any Scripture usage to justify such a meaning.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Bengel:</strong> Formerly there belonged to Messiah, as peculiarly His own , τὰ ἴδια , whatsoever belonged to Israel its land, city, and temple: οἱ ἴδιοι , His own people , the Israelites; [Matthew 8:12] , &ldquo;The …<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Robertson:</strong> Probably here ο ιδιο means the Jewish people, the chosen people to whom Christ was sent first ([Matthew 15:24]), but in a wider sense the whole world is included in ο ιδιο.<br></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv11_0').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Alford's Greek Testament</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1863)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv11_0" class="collapsed comm-body">11. ] τὰ ἴδια here cannot well mean the world , or οἱ ἴδιοι mankind in general: it would be difficult to point out any Scripture usage to justify such a meaning. But abundance of passages bear out the meaning which makes τὰ ἴδια His own inheritance or possession, i.e. Judæa; and οἱ ἴδιοι , the Jews: compare especially the parable [Matthew 21:33] ff., and Sir 24:7 ff. And thus ἦλθεν forms a nearer step in the approach to the declaration in [John 1:14] . He came to His own. On παρέλ . see reff., and above on [John 1:5] .</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv11_1').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Bengel's Gnomon</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1742)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv11_1" class="collapsed comm-body">[John 1:11] . Τὰ ἴδια , His own ) From the world , the whole, the discourse goes down to the part. Formerly there belonged to Messiah, as peculiarly His own , τὰ ἴδια , whatsoever belonged to Israel its land, city, and temple: οἱ ἴδιοι , His own people , the Israelites; [Matthew 8:12] , &ldquo;The children of the kingdom.&rdquo; The time, moreover, of His coming into the world and to His own is one and the same, namely after the coming of John; [John 1:6-7] .</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv11_2').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Robertson's Word Pictures</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1933)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv11_2" class="collapsed comm-body">Unto his own ( εις τα ιδια ). Neuter plural, "unto his own things," the very idiom used in [John 19:27] when the Beloved Disciple took the mother of Jesus "to his own home." The world was "the own home" of the Logos who had made it. See also [John 16:32]; [Acts 21:6]. They that were his own ( ο ιδιο ). In the narrower sense, "his intimates," "his own family," "his own friends" as in [John 13:1]. Jesus later said that a prophet is not without honour save in his own country ([Mark 6:4]; [John 4:44]), and the town of Nazareth where he lived rejected him ([Luke 4:28]; [Matthew 13:58]). Probably here ο ιδιο means the Jewish people, the chosen people to whom Christ was sent first ([Matthew 15:24]), but in a wider sense the whole world is included in ο ιδιο . Conder's The Hebrew Tragedy emphasizes the pathos of the situation that the house of Israel refused to welcome the Messiah when he did come, like a larger and sadder Enoch Arden experience. Received him not ( αυτον ου παρελαβον ). Second aorist active indicative of παραλαμβανω , old verb to take to one's side, common verb to welcome, the very verb used by Jesus in [John 14:3] of the welcome to his Father's house. Cf. κατελαβεν in verse [John 1:5]. Israel slew the Heir ([Hebrews 1:2]) when he came, like the wicked husbandmen ([Luke 20:14]).</div></div><div class="themes-divider">🔍 Temas discutidos</div><div class="theme-card"><div class="theme-word">τὰ ἴδια / οἱ ἴδιοι</div><div class="consensus-bar"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#4caf50">✅ <strong>Alford</strong> τὰ ἴδια significa su herencia/posesión (Judea) y οἱ ἴδιοι los judíos, no el mundo en general</div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#4caf50">✅ <strong>Bengel</strong> τὰ ἴδια se refiere a lo que pertenecía al Mesías (tierra, ciudad, templo de Israel) y οἱ ἴδιοι a los israelitas</div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#ff9800">⚠️ <strong>Robertson</strong> οἱ ἴδιοι probablemente significa el pueblo judío, aunque en sentido amplio incluye todo el mundo</div><div class="theme-summary">Hay consenso en que τὰ ἴδια se refiere a Judea/Israel y οἱ ἴδιοι a los judíos, con Robertson añadiendo una aplicación más amplia.</div></div></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('patr-11')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="patr-11" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">👨‍🏫</span> Patrística · 5 temas · 106 citas <span class="arrow" id="arrow-patr-11">▶</span></div><div id="patr-11" class="collapsed section-content patr-section" role="region"><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt945d4478').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Rechazo de Cristo por su pueblo elegido</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt945d4478" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.11]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"'He came unto His own,'-because all these things were made by Him,-'and His own received Him not.' Who are they? The men whom He made. The Jews whom He at the first made to be above all nations. Because other nations worshipped idols and served demons; but that people was born of the seed of Abraham, and in an eminent sense His own, because kindred through that flesh which He deigned to assume."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.11]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"He came to His own, and His own received Him not, now calling the Jews 'His own,' as His peculiar people, or perhaps even all mankind, as created by Him."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.11]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"For it is a thing indeed worthy of our amazement, how they who were nurtured in knowledge of the prophetical books, who heard Moses every day telling them ten thousand things concerning the coming of the Christ, and the other prophets afterwards, who moreover themselves beheld Christ Himself daily working miracles among them, giving up His time to them alone, neither as yet allowing His disciples to depart into the way of the Gentiles, or to enter into a city of Samaritans, nor doing so Himself"</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres interpretan 'los suyos' principalmente como los judíos, el pueblo elegido que tenía las profecías y prepaación especial, pero también incluyen a toda la humanidad. Su rechazo es especialmente grave dada su preparación privilegiada.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt2ad3b48d').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Bondad divina ante el rechazo humano</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt2ad3b48d" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.11]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Unspeakable of a truth are the riches of the goodness of God, and passing all excess. Consider; 'He came to His own,' not for His personal need, (for, as I said, the Divinity is without wants,) but to do good unto His own people. Yet not even so did His own receive Him, when He came to His own for their advantage, but repelled Him, and not this only, but they even cast Him out of the vineyard, and slew Him. Yet not for this even did He shut them out from repentance, but granted them, if they had"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>John Chrysostom</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Constantinopla, "Boca de Oro", discípulo de Diodoro de Tarso (Antioquía/Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cris%C3%B3stomo" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.11]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"One might wonder at the disciple who is not ashamed of the dishonor of his Teacher, but even records the insolence which was used towards Him: yet this is no small proof of his truth-loving disposition. And besides, he who feels shame should feel it for those who have offered an insult, not for the person outraged. Indeed He by this very thing shone the brighter, as taking, even after the insult, so much care for those who had offered it"</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres destacan la bondad infinita de Dios que vino no por necesidad propia sino para beneficiar a los suyos, y que incluso después del rechazo y crucifixión siguió ofreciendo oportunidades de arrepentimiento. El rechazo revela la gloria divina más que la deshonra.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt16f58978').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Profecías del rechazo de Cristo</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt16f58978" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Cyprian</strong> (c.200-258) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Cartago, mártir, discípulo de Tertuliano (escritos) (Cartago)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cipriano_de_Cartago" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.11]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"That it was previously foretold that they would neither know the Lord, nor understand, nor receive Him. In Isaiah: 'Hear, O heaven, and give ear, O earth: for the Lord hath spoken; I have begotten and brought up children, but they have rejected me. The ox knoweth his owner, and the ass his master's crib: but Israel hath not known me, and my people hath not perceived me. Ah sinful nation, a people filled with sins, a wicked seed, corrupting children: ye have forsaken the Lord, and have sent that'"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> (c.376-444) <span class="patr-meta">— Patriarca de Alejandría, Concilio de Éfeso (Alejandría)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cirilo_de_Alejandr%C3%ADa" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.11]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"The Evangelist pursues his plea that the world did not know its illuminator, that is, the Only Begotten, and from the worse sin of the children of Israel, he hurries to clench the charges against the Gentiles and shows the disease of ignorance alike and unbelief that lay upon the whole world.… For it was not surprising that the world did not know the Only Begotten, he says, seeing that it had left the understanding that befits humanity and was ignorant that it is and was made in honor, being com"</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres ven el rechazo de Cristo como cumplimiento de las profecías del Antiguo Testamento, especialmente de Isaías. El rechazo no fue sorpresivo sino predicho, mostrando tanto la presciencia divina como la culpabilidad humana.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt815bf398').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Encarnación como manifestación visible</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt815bf398" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Augustine of Hippo</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Hipona, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Ambrosio de Milán (Hipona)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agust%C3%ADn_de_Hipona" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.10]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"The Light which lighteneth every man that cometh into the world, came here in the flesh; because while He was here in His Divinity alone, the foolish, blind, and un-righteous could not discern Him; those of whom it is said above, The darkness comprehended it not. Hence the text; He was in the world."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Chrysostom</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.10]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"as in the world, and the world was made by Him' (John i. 10 ): how is He 'brought in,' otherwise than in the flesh?"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>1 Clement</strong> (s.I-II) <span class="patr-meta">— Obispo de Roma, discípulo de Pedro y Pablo (Roma)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clemente_de_Roma" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.11]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"For the Creator of the world is truly the Word of God: and this is our Lord, who in the last times was made man, existing in this world, and who in an invisible manner contains all things created, and is inherent in the entire creation, since the Word of God governs and arranges all things; and therefore He came to His own in a visible manner, and was made flesh, and hung upon the tree, that He might sum up all things in Himself."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres enseñan que la Encarnación fue necesaria para hacer visible al Verbo invisible, permitiendo que los hombres ciegos espiritualmente pudieran percibirlo. La carne fue el medio de manifestación divina al mundo.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt42f1c26c').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Propósito soteriológico de la venida de Cristo</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt42f1c26c" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Maximus the Confessor</strong> (c.580-662) <span class="patr-meta">— Monje teólogo, mártir (mutilado) (Constantinopla)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/M%C3%A1ximo_el_Confesor" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.10]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"[The incarnation of the Logos] is the blessed end on account of which everything was created. This is the divine purpose, which was thought of before the beginning of creation and which we call an intended fulfillment. All creation exists on account of this fulfillment, and yet the fulfillment itself exists because of nothing that was created. Since God had this end in full view, he produced the natures of things."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Thomas Aquinas</strong> (1225-1274) <span class="patr-meta">— Teólogo escolástico, Doctor de la Iglesia, discípulo de Alberto Magno (Italia)</span> <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom%C3%A1s_de_Aquino" target="_blank" class="patr-link">📖</a> <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.11]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Having given the necessity for the incarnation of the Word, the Evangelist then shows the advantage men gained from that incarnation. First, he shows the coming of the light (v 11); secondly, its reception by men (v 11b); thirdly, the fruit brought by the coming of the light (v 12)."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres ven la Encarnación como el propósito eterno de Dios, el fin para el cual fue creado todo. No fue una respuesta al pecado sino el plan divino original para la salvación y perfección de la creación.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="verse-block" id="vb12"><div class="verse-header"><span class="vnum">12</span></div><div class="greek-line" id="greek-12">ὅσοι δὲ ἔλαβον αὐτόν ἔδωκεν αὐτοῖς ἐξουσίαν τέκνα Θεοῦ γενέσθαι τοῖς πιστεύουσιν εἰς τὸ ὄνομα αὐτοῦ</div><div class="uncial-line" id="uncial-12" style="display:none;font-family:'Noto Serif',serif;font-size:0.9rem;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#5d4037;background:#efebe9;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;overflow-wrap:break-word" title="Así se vería este versículo en un manuscrito uncial del siglo IV — todo mayúsculas, sin espacios (puntos medios añadidos como ayuda visual)">ΟΣΟΙ·ΔΕ·ΕΛΑΒΟΝ·ΑΥΤΟΝ·ΕΔΩΚΕΝ·ΑΥΤΟΙΣ·ΕΞΟΥΣΙΑΝ·ΤΕΚΝΑ·ΘΕΟΥ·ΓΕΝΕΣΘΑΙ·ΤΟΙΣ·ΠΙΣΤΕΥΟΥΣΙΝ·ΕΙΣ·ΤΟ·ΟΝΟΜΑ·ΑΥΤΟΥ<span style="display:block;font-size:0.65rem;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:0;opacity:0.7"><a href="https://www.codexsinaiticus.org/en/manuscript.aspx?book=33&chapter=1&verse=12" target="_blank" style="color:#5d4037">Ver en Codex Sinaiticus →</a></span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:0.3rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:0.3rem;align-items:center"><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="toggleRVR(12)">RVR60</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('uncial-12').style.display=document.getElementById('uncial-12').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#efebe9;color:#5d4037;border-color:#bcaaa4" title="Escritura uncial: así se veía el NT en los manuscritos del s.IV (Vaticanus, Sinaiticus). Todo mayúsculas, sin espacios entre palabras (scriptio continua), sin acentos ni puntuación. La iota subscrita se escribe explícitamente.">Uncial</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('pron-12').style.display=document.getElementById('pron-12').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0;border-color:#90caf9" title="Pronunciación bizantina aproximada (griego moderno/eclesiástico)">Pronunciación</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-patr" onclick="toggleSection('patr-12')" title="33 citas patrísticas disponibles">✝ 33 patrística</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-exeg" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-12')" title="3 comentarios exegéticos">📚 3 exégesis</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-ver" onclick="document.getElementById('vers-12').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="9 versiones disponibles">📖 versiones</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('xrefs-12').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="8 referencias cruzadas">🔗 8 refs</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="copyVerse(12)" title="Copiar versículo al portapapeles" style="background:#f3e5f5;border-color:#ce93d8;color:#6a1b9a">📋</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('notes-12').style.display=document.getElementById('notes-12').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" title="Notas personales" style="background:#fff8e1;border-color:#ffd54f;color:#f57f17">📝</div></div><div id="rvr-12" class="collapsed spanish-line">Mas a todos los que le recibieron, a los que creen en su nombre, les dio potestad de ser hechos hijos de Dios;</div><div id="vers-12" class="collapsed" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR60</span>Mas a todos los que le recibieron, a los que creen en su nombre, les dio potestad de ser hechos hijos de Dios;</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR1909</span>Mas á todos los que le recibieron, dióles potestad de ser hechos hijos de Dios, á los que creen en su nombre:</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">KJV</span>But as many as received him, to them gave he power to become the sons of God, even to them that believe on his name:</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">ASV</span>But as many as received him, to them gave he the right to become children of God, even to them that believe on his name: </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">BSB</span>But to all who did receive Him, to those who believed in His name, He gave the right to become children of God— </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Darby</span>but as many as received him, to them gave he [the] right to be children ofGod, to those that believe on his name; </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">LITV</span>But as many as received Him, to them He gave authority to become children of God, to the ones believing into His name, </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">YLT</span>but as many as did receive him to them he gave authority to become sons of God--to those believing in his name,</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Vulgate</span>quotquot autem receperunt eum dedit eis potestatem filios Dei fieri his qui credunt in nomine eius</div></div><div id="xrefs-12" class="collapsed xref-container" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 John 3:1" data-es="MIRAD cuál amor nos ha dado el Padre, que seamos llamados hijos de Dios: por esto el mundo no nos conoce, porque no le conoce á él." data-gr="ἴδετε ποταπὴν ἀγάπην δέδωκεν ἡμῖν ὁ πατὴρ ἵνα τέκνα θεοῦ κληθῶμεν, ⸂καὶ ἐσμέν⸃. διὰ τοῦτο ὁ κόσμος οὐ γινώσκει ⸀ἡμᾶς ὅτι οὐκ ἔγνω αὐτόν." data-lxx="" title="MIRAD cuál amor nos ha dado el Padre, que seamos llamados hijos de Dios: por est…">1 John 3:1</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 John 3:23" data-es="Y éste es su mandamiento: Que creamos en el nombre de su Hijo Jesucristo, y nos amemos unos á otros como nos lo ha mandado." data-gr="καὶ αὕτη ἐστὶν ἡ ἐντολὴ αὐτοῦ, ἵνα ⸀πιστεύσωμεν τῷ ὀνόματι τοῦ υἱοῦ αὐτοῦ Ἰησοῦ Χριστοῦ καὶ ἀγαπῶμεν ἀλλήλους, καθὼς ἔδωκεν ἐντολὴν ⸀ἡμῖν." data-lxx="" title="Y éste es su mandamiento: Que creamos en el nombre de su Hijo Jesucristo, y nos …">1 John 3:23</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 John 5:12" data-es="El que tiene al Hijo, tiene al vida: el que no tiene la Hijo de Dios, no tiene la vida." data-gr="ὁ ἔχων τὸν υἱὸν ἔχει τὴν ζωήν· ὁ μὴ ἔχων τὸν υἱὸν τοῦ θεοῦ τὴν ζωὴν οὐκ ἔχει." data-lxx="" title="El que tiene al Hijo, tiene al vida: el que no tiene la Hijo de Dios, no tiene l…">1 John 5:12</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 John 5:13" data-es="Estas cosas he escrito á vosotros que creéis en el nombre del Hijo de Dios, para que sepáis que tenéis vida eterna, y para que creáis en el nombre del Hijo de Dios." data-gr="Ταῦτα ἔγραψα ⸀ὑμῖν ἵνα εἰδῆτε ὅτι ζωὴν ⸂ἔχετε αἰώνιον⸃, ⸂τοῖς πιστεύουσιν⸃ εἰς τὸ ὄνομα τοῦ υἱοῦ τοῦ θεοῦ." data-lxx="" title="Estas cosas he escrito á vosotros que creéis en el nombre del Hijo de Dios, para…">1 John 5:13</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="2 Corinthians 6:17" data-es="Por lo cual Salid de en medio de ellos, y apartaos, dice el Señor, Y no toquéis lo inmundo; Y yo os recibiré," data-gr="διὸ ἐξέλθατε ἐκ μέσου αὐτῶν, καὶ ἀφορίσθητε, λέγει κύριος, καὶ ἀκαθάρτου μὴ ἅπτεσθε· κἀγὼ εἰσδέξομαι ὑμᾶς·" data-lxx="" title="Por lo cual Salid de en medio de ellos, y apartaos, dice el Señor, Y no toquéis …">2 Corinthians 6:17</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="2 Corinthians 6:18" data-es="Y seré á vosotros Padre, Y vosotros me seréis á mí hijos é hijas, dice el Señor Todopoderoso." data-gr="καὶ ἔσομαι ὑμῖν εἰς πατέρα, καὶ ὑμεῖς ἔσεσθέ μοι εἰς υἱοὺς καὶ θυγατέρας, λέγει κύριος παντοκράτωρ." data-lxx="" title="Y seré á vosotros Padre, Y vosotros me seréis á mí hijos é hijas, dice el Señor …">2 Corinthians 6:18</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="2 Peter 1:4" data-es="Por las cuales nos son dadas preciosas y grandísimas promesas, para que por ellas fueseis hechos participantes de la naturaleza divina, habiendo huído de la corrupción que está en el mundo por concupiscencia." data-gr="δι’ ὧν τὰ ⸂τίμια καὶ μέγιστα ἡμῖν⸃ ἐπαγγέλματα δεδώρηται, ἵνα διὰ τούτων γένησθε θείας κοινωνοὶ φύσεως, ἀποφυγόντες τῆς ἐν ⸀τῷ κόσμῳ ἐν ἐπιθυμίᾳ φθορᾶς." data-lxx="" title="Por las cuales nos son dadas preciosas y grandísimas promesas, para que por ella…">2 Peter 1:4</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="Acts 3:16" data-es="Y en la fe de su nombre, á éste que vosotros veis y conocéis, ha confirmado su nombre: y la fe que por él es, ha dado á este esta completa sanidad en presencia de todos vosotros." data-gr="καὶ ⸀ἐπὶ τῇ πίστει τοῦ ὀνόματος αὐτοῦ τοῦτον ὃν θεωρεῖτε καὶ οἴδατε ἐστερέωσεν τὸ ὄνομα αὐτοῦ, καὶ ἡ πίστις ἡ δι’ αὐτοῦ ἔδωκεν αὐτῷ τὴν ὁλοκληρίαν ταύτην ἀπέναντι πάντων ὑμῶν." data-lxx="" title="Y en la fe de su nombre, á éste que vosotros veis y conocéis, ha confirmado su n…">Acts 3:16</span></div><div id="pron-12" style="display:none;font-size:0.85rem;color:#1565c0;background:#e3f2fd;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;font-style:italic" class="pron-line"></div><div id="notes-12" style="display:none;margin-bottom:0.5rem"><textarea id="note-input-12" style="width:100%;min-height:50px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;padding:4px 8px;font-size:0.82rem;resize:vertical" placeholder="Tus notas para v.12..." oninput="saveNote(12)"></textarea></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-12')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="exeg-12" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">📜</span> Exégesis del Griego <span class="arrow" id="arrow-exeg-12">▶</span></div><div id="exeg-12" class="collapsed section-content exeg-section" role="region"><div class="exeg-summary"><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Alford:</strong> ] The ὅσοι … primarily refers to the ἐκλογή among the Jews who have just been spoken of: but also, by implication, being opposed to both ὁ κόσμος and οἱ ἴδιοι , the ἐκλογή in all the world.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Bengel:</strong> Παραλαμβάνειν was the part of the Jews, whom the Truth was appertaining to [spectabat]; λαμβάνειν is the part also of the Gentiles, whom grace appertaineth to [spectat].<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Robertson:</strong> In [John 5:27] εδωκεν (first aorist active indicative of διδωμ ) εξουσιαν means authority but includes power ( δυναμις ).<br></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv12_0').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Alford's Greek Testament</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1863)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv12_0" class="collapsed comm-body">12. ] The ὅσοι … primarily refers to the ἐκλογή among the Jews who have just been spoken of: but also, by implication, being opposed to both ὁ κόσμος and οἱ ἴδιοι , the ἐκλογή in all the world. ἔλαβον = παρέλαβον above as many as recognized Him as that which He was the Word of God and Light of men. ἔδωκεν αὐτ . ἐξουσ . ] ἐξουσ . is not merely capability = δύναμιν (Lücke), still less privilege or prerogative (Chrysost. and others), but power (De Wette); involving all the actions and states needful to their so becoming, and removing all the obstacles in their way (e.g. the wrath of God, and the guilt of sin). τέκνα θ . γενέσθαι ] The spiritual life owes its beginning to a birth from above , ch. [John 3:3-7] . And this birth is owing to the Holy Spirit of God; so that this is equivalent to saying, &lsquo;As many as received Him, to them gave He His Holy Spirit.&rsquo; And we find that it was so: see [Acts 10:44] . τέκνα θ . is a more comprehensive expression than υἱοὶ τ . θ ., which brings out rather our adoption , and hope of inheritance ([Romans 8:14] ff.), whereas the other involves the whole generation and process of our life in the Spirit, as being from and of God, and consequently our likeness to God, walking in light as He is in light ( 1Jn 1:5-7 ) free from sin (ib. [1 John 3:9] ; Joh 5:18 ) and death (ch. Joh 8:51 ). τοῖς πιστ . εἰς τ . ὄν . αὐτ . ] τὸ ὄνομα αὐτ . is His manifestation as that which He has given Himself out to be , i.e. as a Saviour from sin: see [Matthew 1:21] , καλέσεις τὸ ὄνομα αὐτοῦ Ἰησοῦν · αὐτὸς γὰρ σώσει τὸν λαὸν αὐτοῦ ἀπὸ τῶν ἁμαρτιῶν αὐτῶν .</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv12_1').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Bengel's Gnomon</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1742)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv12_1" class="collapsed comm-body">[John 1:12] . Ὅσοι , as many as ) even [including also] such as previously had not been ἴδιοι , His own . ἔλαβον ) This verb differs from καταλαμβάνειν , [John 1:5] , and from παραλαμβάνειν , [John 1:11] . Καταλαμβανω is applied to that which is close by: παραλαμβάνω , that which is offered: λαμβάνω , of my own accord. Παραλαμβάνειν was the part of the Jews, whom the Truth was appertaining to [spectabat]; λαμβάνειν is the part also of the Gentiles, whom grace appertaineth to [spectat]. In Joh 1:12-13 mere external differences are taken away most effectually. [Galatians 3:26] , etc., &ldquo;For ye are all the children of God by faith in Christ Jesus.&rdquo; ἔδωκεν , He gave ) This is the Glory of Christ, the Only-begotten Son. It belongs to the Divine authority to make Sons OF GOD: as it belongs to the Light, to make sons of light, ch. [John 12:36] , &ldquo;Believe in the Light, that ye may be the children of light.&rdquo; ἐξουσίαν , power ) The power [17] does not precede the γένεσιν τέκνων or filiation, as if they were two distinct things: but the filiation itself is this power, or, in other words, dignity. A great fact! [John 8:36] . [18] τέκνα Θεοῦ τοῖς πιστεύουσιν ,) sons OF GOD to them that believe ) Two weighty truths are set before us, of which the former is elucidated in [John 1:13] ; the second in [John 1:14] , where the manifestation of the Word in the flesh is not so much recorded as it was accomplished, but rather as it was believed: which view the series of things down from Joh 1:6 proves. γἐνεσθαι , to become ) whereas Jesus is the Son of God. ὄνομα , the name ) The name of the Only-begotten. For to this is to be referred [John 1:14] . The connection is inferred from the kindred term τέκνα , children [ sons ]. [17] Potestas, legitimate power, authority; not mere δύναμις , potentia, might . E. and T. [18] If the Son, therefore, shall make you free, ye shall be free indeed. Comp. [Galatians 4:6] . E. and T.</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv12_2').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Robertson's Word Pictures</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1933)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv12_2" class="collapsed comm-body">As many as received him ( οσο ελαβον αυτον ). Effective aorist active indicative of λαμβανω "as many as did receive him," in contrast with ο ιδιο just before, exceptional action on the part of the disciples and other believers. To them ( αυτοις ). Dative case explanatory of the relative clause preceding, an anacoluthon common in John 27 times as against 21 in the Synoptists. This is a common Aramaic idiom and is urged by Burney (Aramaic Origin, etc., p. 64) for his theory of an Aramaic original of the Fourth Gospel. The right ( εξουσιαν ). In [John 5:27] εδωκεν (first aorist active indicative of διδωμ ) εξουσιαν means authority but includes power ( δυναμις ). Here it is more the notion of privilege or right. To become ( γενεσθα ). Second aorist middle of γινομα , to become what they were not before. Children of God ( τεκνα θεου ). In the full spiritual sense, not as mere offspring of God true of all men ([Acts 17:28]). Paul's phrase υιο θεου ([Galatians 3:26]) for believers, used also by Jesus of the pure in heart ([Matthew 5:9]), does not occur in John's Gospel (but in [Revelation 21:7]). It is possible that John prefers τα τεκνα του θεου for the spiritual children of God whether Jew or Gentile ([John 11:52]) because of the community of nature ( τεκνον from root τεκ- , to beget). But one cannot follow Westcott in insisting on "adoption" as Paul's reason for the use of υιο since Jesus uses υιο θεου in [Matthew 5:9]. Clearly the idea of regeneration is involved here as in [John 3:3]. Even to them that believe ( τοις πιστευουσιν ). No "even" in the Greek, merely explanatory apposition with αυτοις , dative case of the articular present active participle of πιστευω . On his name ( εις το ονομα ). Bernard notes πιστευω εις 35 times in John, to put trust in or on. See also [John 2:23]; [John 3:38] for πιστευω εις το ονομα αυτου . This common use of ονομα for the person is an Aramaism, but it occurs also in the vernacular papyri and εις το ονομα is particularly common in the payment of debts (Moulton and Milligan's Vocabulary). See [Acts 1:15] for ονοματα for persons.</div></div><div class="themes-divider">🔍 Temas discutidos</div><div class="theme-card"><div class="theme-word">ἔλαβον vs παρέλαβον</div><div class="consensus-bar"><div style="width:55%;background:#ff9800"></div></div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#4caf50">✅ <strong>Alford</strong> ἔλαβον equivale a παρέλαβον, significando reconocerlo como la Palabra de Dios</div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#f44336">❌ <strong>Bengel</strong> λαμβάνω difiere de καταλαμβάνειν y παραλαμβάνειν - λαμβάνω implica acción voluntaria propia</div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#ff9800">⚠️ <strong>Robertson</strong> ἔλαβον indica acción efectiva de recibir en contraste con el rechazo anterior</div><div class="theme-summary">Bengel distingue matices específicos entre los verbos, mientras Alford los equipara y Robertson enfatiza el contraste contextual.</div></div><div class="theme-card"><div class="theme-word">ἐξουσίαν</div><div class="consensus-bar"><div style="width:55%;background:#ff9800"></div></div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#4caf50">✅ <strong>Alford</strong> ἐξουσίαν es poder (no mera capacidad o privilegio) que remueve obstáculos como la ira de Dios</div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#f44336">❌ <strong>Robertson</strong> En Juan 5:27 ἐξουσίαν significa autoridad pero incluye poder, aquí es más la noción de privilegio o derecho</div><div class="theme-summary">Alford enfatiza el aspecto de poder efectivo, mientras Robertson ve más el aspecto de privilegio o derecho.</div></div></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('patr-12')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="patr-12" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">👨‍🏫</span> Patrística · 5 temas · 33 citas <span class="arrow" id="arrow-patr-12">▶</span></div><div id="patr-12" class="collapsed section-content patr-section" role="region"><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pte2f83788').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Adopción divina y filiación por gracia</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pte2f83788" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Atanasio de Alejandría</strong> (c.296-373) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.12]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"But this is God's kindness to man, that of whom He is Maker, of them according to grace He afterwards becomes Father also; becomes, that is, when men, His creatures, receive into their hearts, as the Apostle says, 'the Spirit of His Son, crying, Abba, Father.' And these are they who, having received the Word, gained power from Him to become sons of God; for they could not become sons, being by nature creatures, otherwise than by receiving the Spirit of the natural and true Son."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Agustín de Hipona</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.12]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"I mean, you are not being told not to be a human, in the sense that you are to be a beast, but rather that you are to be among those to whom 'he gave the right to become children of God.' God, you see, wants to make you a god; not by nature, of course, like the one whom he begot; but by his gift and by adoption. For just as he through being humbled came to share your mortality; so through lifting you up he brings you to share his immortality."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Juan Crisóstomo</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.12]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"'As many as received Him, to them gave He power to become sons of God.' Whether bond or free, whether Greeks or barbarians or Scythians, unlearned or learned, female or male, children or old men, in honor or dishonor, rich or poor, rulers or private persons, all, He saith, are deemed worthy the same privilege; for faith and the grace of the Spirit, removing the inequality caused by worldly things, hath moulded all to one fashion, and stamped them with one impress, the King's."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Tertuliano</strong> (c.160-225) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.12]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"The prayer begins with a testimony to God, and with the reward of faith, when we say, 'Our Father who art in the heavens;' for (in so saying), we at once pray to God, and commend faith, whose reward this appellation is. It is written, 'To them who believed on Him He gave power to be called sons of God.'"</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres enseñan unánimemente que la filiación divina es un don de gracia, no natural, otorgado a quienes reciben a Cristo por fe. Esta adopción trasciende todas las distinciones sociales y étnicas.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt1f20ef1f').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Necesidad del esfuerzo humano tras el bautismo</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt1f20ef1f" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Juan Crisóstomo</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.12]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Why then did he say not that 'He made them sons of God,' but that 'He gave them power to become sons of God'? To show that we need much zeal to keep the image of sonship impressed on us at Baptism, all through without spot or soils; and at the same time to show that no one shall be able to take this power from us, unless we are the first to deprive ourselves of it."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Juan Crisóstomo</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.12]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Having therefore everywhere excluded compulsion and pointing to (man's) voluntary choice and free power, he has said the same now. For even in these mystical blessings, it is, on the one hand, God's part, to give the grace, on the other, man's to supply faith; and in after time there needs for what remains much earnestness."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres enfatizan que aunque Dios otorga el poder de ser hijos, se requiere esfuerzo continuo del creyente para mantener esta dignidad. La cooperación humana es esencial tanto en la fe inicial como en la perseverancia.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pteede4799').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Universalidad de la salvación</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pteede4799" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Juan Crisóstomo</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.12]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"'As many as received Him, to them gave He power to become sons of God.' Whether bond or free, whether Greeks or barbarians or Scythians, unlearned or learned, female or male, children or old men, in honor or dishonor, rich or poor, rulers or private persons, all, He saith, are deemed worthy the same privilege"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Cirilo de Alejandría</strong> (c.376-444) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.12]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"A right judgement verily and worthy of God! The firstborn, Israel, is cast out; for he would not abide in ownness with God, nor did he receive the Son, Who came among His own, he rejected the Bestower of Nobility, he thrust away the Giver of Grace: the Gentiles received Him by faith."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Tomás de Aquino</strong> (1225-1274) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.12]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"However, there were not lacking those who did receive him. Hence he adds, but whoever received him. The Evangelist uses this manner of speaking, saying, but whoever, to indicate that the deliverance would be more extensive than the promise, which had been made only to his own, i.e., to the Jews."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres enseñan que la salvación se extiende más allá de Israel a todos los pueblos. La filiación divina está disponible para cualquiera que reciba a Cristo, sin distinción de raza o condición social.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt9cfb1ac3').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Transformación bautismal</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt9cfb1ac3" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Juan Crisóstomo</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.12]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"And as the element of fire, when it meets with ore from the mine, straightway of earth makes it gold, even so and much more Baptism makes those who are washed to be of gold instead of clay; the Spirit at that time falling like fire into our souls, burning up the 'image of the earthy' (1 Cor. xv. 49), and producing 'the image of the heavenly,' fresh coined, bright and glittering, as from the furnace-mould."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Basilio de Cesarea</strong> (c.330-379) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.12]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"When the soul has been clothed with the Son of God, it becomes worthy of the final and perfect stage and is baptized in the name of the Father himself of our Lord Jesus Christ, who, according to the testimony of John, gave the power to be made the sons of God."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres describen el bautismo como una transformación radical del alma, comparándola con el fuego que convierte el mineral en oro. El alma se reviste de Cristo y adquiere la dignidad filial.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('ptb76c814e').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Encarnación y divinización mutua</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="ptb76c814e" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Juan Crisóstomo</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.12]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Having declared that they who received Him were 'born of God,' and had become 'sons of God,' he adds the cause and reason of this unspeakable honor. It is that 'the Word became Flesh,' that the Master took on Him the form of a servant. For He became Son of man, who was God's own Son, in order that He might make the sons of men to be children of God."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Ireneo</strong> (c.130-202) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.13]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"For it was for this end that the Word of God was made man, and He who was the Son of God became the Son of man, that man, having been taken into the Word, and receiving the adoption, might become the son of God. For by no other means could we have attained to incorruptibility and immortality, unless we had been united to incorruptibility and immortality."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Teodoreto de Ciro</strong> (c.393-458) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.12]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"For this is why the Word became a human being and the Son of God became a Son of man: that the human being, by embracing the Word and receiving adoption, might become"</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres enseñan el intercambio admirable: Cristo se hizo hombre para que los hombres pudieran hacerse hijos de Dios. La encarnación es el fundamento de la divinización humana.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="verse-block" id="vb13"><div class="verse-header"><span class="vnum">13</span></div><div class="greek-line" id="greek-13">οἳ οὐκ ἐξ αἱμάτων οὐδὲ ἐκ θελήματος σαρκὸς οὐδὲ ἐκ θελήματος ἀνδρὸς ἀλλ᾽ ἐκ Θεοῦ ἐγεννήθησαν</div><div class="uncial-line" id="uncial-13" style="display:none;font-family:'Noto Serif',serif;font-size:0.9rem;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#5d4037;background:#efebe9;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;overflow-wrap:break-word" title="Así se vería este versículo en un manuscrito uncial del siglo IV — todo mayúsculas, sin espacios (puntos medios añadidos como ayuda visual)">ΟΙ·ΟΥΚ·ΕΞ·ΑΙΜΑΤΩΝ·ΟΥΔΕ·ΕΚ·ΘΕΛΗΜΑΤΟΣ·ΣΑΡΚΟΣ·ΟΥΔΕ·ΕΚ·ΘΕΛΗΜΑΤΟΣ·ΑΝΔΡΟΣ·ΑΛΛ·ΕΚ·ΘΕΟΥ·ΕΓΕΝΝΗΘΗΣΑΝ<span style="display:block;font-size:0.65rem;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:0;opacity:0.7"><a href="https://www.codexsinaiticus.org/en/manuscript.aspx?book=33&chapter=1&verse=13" target="_blank" style="color:#5d4037">Ver en Codex Sinaiticus →</a></span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:0.3rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:0.3rem;align-items:center"><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="toggleRVR(13)">RVR60</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('uncial-13').style.display=document.getElementById('uncial-13').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#efebe9;color:#5d4037;border-color:#bcaaa4" title="Escritura uncial: así se veía el NT en los manuscritos del s.IV (Vaticanus, Sinaiticus). Todo mayúsculas, sin espacios entre palabras (scriptio continua), sin acentos ni puntuación. La iota subscrita se escribe explícitamente.">Uncial</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('pron-13').style.display=document.getElementById('pron-13').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0;border-color:#90caf9" title="Pronunciación bizantina aproximada (griego moderno/eclesiástico)">Pronunciación</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-patr" onclick="toggleSection('patr-13')" title="22 citas patrísticas disponibles">✝ 22 patrística</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-exeg" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-13')" title="3 comentarios exegéticos">📚 3 exégesis</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-ver" onclick="document.getElementById('vers-13').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="9 versiones disponibles">📖 versiones</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('xrefs-13').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="8 referencias cruzadas">🔗 8 refs</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="copyVerse(13)" title="Copiar versículo al portapapeles" style="background:#f3e5f5;border-color:#ce93d8;color:#6a1b9a">📋</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('notes-13').style.display=document.getElementById('notes-13').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" title="Notas personales" style="background:#fff8e1;border-color:#ffd54f;color:#f57f17">📝</div></div><div id="rvr-13" class="collapsed spanish-line">los cuales no son engendrados de sangre, ni de voluntad de carne, ni de voluntad de varón, sino de Dios.</div><div id="vers-13" class="collapsed" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR60</span>los cuales no son engendrados de sangre, ni de voluntad de carne, ni de voluntad de varón, sino de Dios.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR1909</span>Los cuales no son engendrados de sangre, ni de voluntad de carne, ni de voluntad de varón, mas de Dios.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">KJV</span>Which were born, not of blood, nor of the will of the flesh, nor of the will of man, but of God.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">ASV</span>who were born, not of blood, nor of the will of the flesh, nor of the will of man, but of God. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">BSB</span>children born not of blood, nor of the desire or will of man, but born of God. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Darby</span>who have been born, not of blood, nor of flesh's will, nor of man's will, but ofGod. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">LITV</span>who were born not of bloods, nor of the will of the flesh, nor of the will of man, but were born of God. </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">YLT</span>who--not of blood nor of a will of flesh, nor of a will of man but--of God were begotten.</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Vulgate</span>qui non ex sanguinibus neque ex voluntate carnis neque ex voluntate viri sed ex Deo nati sunt</div></div><div id="xrefs-13" class="collapsed xref-container" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 Corinthians 3:6" data-es="Yo planté, Apolos regó: mas Dios ha dado el crecimiento." data-gr="ἐγὼ ἐφύτευσα, Ἀπολλῶς ἐπότισεν, ἀλλὰ ὁ θεὸς ηὔξανεν·" data-lxx="" title="Yo planté, Apolos regó: mas Dios ha dado el crecimiento.">1 Corinthians 3:6</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 John 2:28" data-es="Y ahora, hijitos, perseverad en él; para que cuando apareciere, tengamos confianza, y no seamos confundidos de él en su venida." data-gr="Καὶ νῦν, τεκνία, μένετε ἐν αὐτῷ, ἵνα ⸀ἐὰν φανερωθῇ ⸀σχῶμεν παρρησίαν καὶ μὴ αἰσχυνθῶμεν ἀπ’ αὐτοῦ ἐν τῇ παρουσίᾳ αὐτοῦ." data-lxx="" title="Y ahora, hijitos, perseverad en él; para que cuando apareciere, tengamos confian…">1 John 2:28</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 John 2:29" data-es="Si sabéis que él es justo, sabed también que cualquiera que hace justicia, es nacido de él." data-gr="ἐὰν εἰδῆτε ὅτι δίκαιός ἐστιν, γινώσκετε ⸀ὅτι πᾶς ὁ ποιῶν τὴν δικαιοσύνην ἐξ αὐτοῦ γεγέννηται." data-lxx="" title="Si sabéis que él es justo, sabed también que cualquiera que hace justicia, es na…">1 John 2:29</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 John 3:9" data-es="Cualquiera que es nacido de Dios, no hace pecado, porque su simiente está en él; y no puede pecar, porque es nacido de Dios." data-gr="πᾶς ὁ γεγεννημένος ἐκ τοῦ θεοῦ ἁμαρτίαν οὐ ποιεῖ, ὅτι σπέρμα αὐτοῦ ἐν αὐτῷ μένει, καὶ οὐ δύναται ἁμαρτάνειν, ὅτι ἐκ τοῦ θεοῦ γεγέννηται." data-lxx="" title="Cualquiera que es nacido de Dios, no hace pecado, porque su simiente está en él;…">1 John 3:9</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 John 4:7" data-es="Carísimos, amémonos unos á otros; porque el amor es de Dios. Cualquiera que ama, es nacido de Dios, y conoce á Dios." data-gr="Ἀγαπητοί, ἀγαπῶμεν ἀλλήλους, ὅτι ἡ ἀγάπη ἐκ τοῦ θεοῦ ἐστιν, καὶ πᾶς ὁ ἀγαπῶν ἐκ τοῦ θεοῦ γεγέννηται καὶ γινώσκει τὸν θεόν." data-lxx="" title="Carísimos, amémonos unos á otros; porque el amor es de Dios. Cualquiera que ama,…">1 John 4:7</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 John 5:4" data-es="Porque todo aquello que es nacido de Dios vence al mundo: y esta es la victoria que vence al mundo, nuestra fe." data-gr="ὅτι πᾶν τὸ γεγεννημένον ἐκ τοῦ θεοῦ νικᾷ τὸν κόσμον. καὶ αὕτη ἐστὶν ἡ νίκη ἡ νικήσασα τὸν κόσμον, ἡ πίστις ἡμῶν·" data-lxx="" title="Porque todo aquello que es nacido de Dios vence al mundo: y esta es la victoria …">1 John 5:4</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 Peter 1:23" data-es="Siendo renacidos, no de simiente corruptible, sino de incorruptible, por la palabra de Dios, que vive y permanece para siempre." data-gr="ἀναγεγεννημένοι οὐκ ἐκ σπορᾶς φθαρτῆς ἀλλὰ ἀφθάρτου, διὰ λόγου ζῶντος θεοῦ καὶ ⸀μένοντος·" data-lxx="" title="Siendo renacidos, no de simiente corruptible, sino de incorruptible, por la pala…">1 Peter 1:23</span><span class="xref-pill" onclick="showXrefPopup(this)" data-ref="1 Peter 1:3" data-es="Bendito el Dios y Padre de nuestro Señor Jesucristo, que según su grande misericordia nos ha regenerado en esperanza viva, por la resurrección de Jesucristo de los muertos," data-gr="Εὐλογητὸς ὁ θεὸς καὶ πατὴρ τοῦ κυρίου ἡμῶν Ἰησοῦ Χριστοῦ, ὁ κατὰ τὸ πολὺ αὐτοῦ ἔλεος ἀναγεννήσας ἡμᾶς εἰς ἐλπίδα ζῶσαν δι’ ἀναστάσεως Ἰησοῦ Χριστοῦ ἐκ νεκρῶν," data-lxx="" title="Bendito el Dios y Padre de nuestro Señor Jesucristo, que según su grande miseric…">1 Peter 1:3</span></div><div id="pron-13" style="display:none;font-size:0.85rem;color:#1565c0;background:#e3f2fd;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;font-style:italic" class="pron-line"></div><div id="notes-13" style="display:none;margin-bottom:0.5rem"><textarea id="note-input-13" style="width:100%;min-height:50px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;padding:4px 8px;font-size:0.82rem;resize:vertical" placeholder="Tus notas para v.13..." oninput="saveNote(13)"></textarea></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-13')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="exeg-13" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">📜</span> Exégesis del Griego <span class="arrow" id="arrow-exeg-13">▶</span></div><div id="exeg-13" class="collapsed section-content exeg-section" role="region"><div class="exeg-summary"><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Alford:</strong> ἐκ , remarks De Wette, denotes, the first time, the material the second and third time, the mediate cause, the fourth time, the immediate cause, of the generation.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Bengel:</strong> For as the words [ ἐλαβον ] received and to them that believe [ τοῖς πιστεύουσιν ] correspond to one another, and denote the cause: so the effect is denoted in that expression to become children , and…<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Robertson:</strong> , though why it is not clear unless blood of both father and mother; εκ θεληματος σαρκος , from sexual desire; εκ θεληματος ανδρος , from the will of the male).<br></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv13_0').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Alford's Greek Testament</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1863)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv13_0" class="collapsed comm-body">13. ] The Jews grounded their claim to be children of God on their descent from Abraham. John here negatives any such claim, and asserts the exclusive divine birth of all who become children of God by faith. It is to be noticed that the conjunctions here are not the merely disjunctive ones οὔτε … οὔτε , which would necessitate the ranging the clauses as co-ordinate and parallel, but οὐδὲ … οὐδέ , which rise in climax from one clause to another, &lsquo; not ἐξ αἱμάτων , nor yet ἐκ θελ . σαρκ . nor yet ἐκ θελ . ἀνδ ., but ἐκ θεοῦ &rsquo; (see examples of οὔτε , [Matthew 12:32] ; of οὐδέ , Mat 6:26 ). Many interpreters have seen in θέλημα ἀνδρός the male, and in θέλημα σαρκός the female side of human concupiscence (so Augustine, Theophylact, &c.); or in the former the higher and more conscious, in the latter the lower and animal side (Bleek, Luthardt). Besides the above, other objections lie against both these interpretations, (1) that σάρξ is never so used ( Eph 5:29 is no instance in point); (2) that θέλημα is ascribed to both . Euthymius seems to give the right interpretation: εἰπὼν δὲ ὅτι οὐκ ἐξ αἱμάτων , ἐπήγαγε φανερώτερον ὅτι οὐδὲ ἐκ θελήματος σαρκός · εἶτα καὶ τοῦτο τελεώτερον ἐφηρμήνευσε , προσθεὶς ὅτι οὐκ ἐκ θελήματος ἀνδρός · αἷμα γὰρ καὶ σάρξ , ὁ ἀνήρ · θέλημα δὲ νῦν νοεῖ τὴν ἐπιθυμίαν , τὴν συνουσίαν : in loc. ii. 421. Or perhaps this may be earned somewhat further, and we may better satisfy the climax by regarding the ἐξ αἱμάτων as indicating the mere phenomena of physical generation wherever found: then rising to ἐκ θελήματος σαρκός , the instigation of that capacity by sexual desire: then rising still higher to the most exalted instance of that desire, ἐκ θελήματος ἀνδρός . The plural usage of αἱμάτων is only found in one other place in this signification, Eurip. Ion 693 Dind., 705 Herm., ἔχει δόλον τύχαν θ ʼ ὁ παῖς | ἄλλων τραφεὶς ἀφ ʼ αἱμάτων . The other usage of the plural, for murder , is frequent in the LXX and the classics. ἀνήρ , in the sense of man generally, is not uncommon; we have in plur. πατὴρ ἀνδρῶν τε θεῶν τε , in Hom. passim; and in sing. Il. ν . 321; σ . 432, 433. ἐκ , remarks De Wette, denotes, the first time, the material the second and third time, the mediate cause, the fourth time, the immediate cause, of the generation.</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv13_1').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Bengel's Gnomon</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1742)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv13_1" class="collapsed comm-body">[John 1:13] . Οἱ , who ) This is to be referred to τέκνα , children . For as the words [ ἐλαβον ] received and to them that believe [ τοῖς πιστεύουσιν ] correspond to one another, and denote the cause: so the effect is denoted in that expression to become children , and it is further explained in this verse. οὐκ ἐξ αἱμάτων , not of bloods ) דמים αἵματα , the Hebrew idiom often has bloods in the Plural number, even when only one man is spoken of: but when the subject treated of is generation, it does not call it the blood or bloods of the parents. But for the commendation of a noble lineage, the term blood is frequent among the ancient writers, as it is in the usage of the present day: and thence it is that bloods denote variety of origins, in consequence of which various prerogatives [privileges] are either sought after, or even enjoyed, in the world. οὐδε ἐκ θελήματος σαρκός , nor of the will of the flesh) Husband and wife are Flesh, and that one flesh: and the will of the wedded pair, חפץ , gives birth to the children, who being born of the flesh are flesh, and sons of the flesh. [John 3:6] , &ldquo;That which is born of the flesh is flesh;&rdquo; [Romans 9:8] , &ldquo;They which are the children of the flesh, these are not the children of God.&rdquo; With propriety the term, the will, is used as moving midway between holy [pure] love, and grovelling lust, ὄρεξιν . Nor does John use the softer word, of which the flesh considered in itself is unworthy: nor the harsher, lest those born of holy [pure] parents should except themselves [i.e. Had John said, The children of God were born not of lust, then those men who are born of a pure marriage union might think themselves excepted from the children of the flesh]. οὐδὲ ἐκ θελήματος ἀνδρός , nor of the will of man) The will of man is contained in the will of the flesh: and yet it is mentioned separately, as if it were the greater, and in some measure, the more guilty part of it. For Christ had a mother, but one who knew not man. [Luke 1:34] , &ldquo;How shall this be, seeing I know not a man.&rdquo; [Mary to the angel]. These three things, bloods, the will of the flesh, the will of man , bring to the sons of men ἐξουσίαν , power and rank , which are noble, but natural and human. For, indeed, it was on these three the Jews used to lean, being wont to boast either of their ancestors , Abraham, Isaac, Israel, Juda, Benjamin, Levi, Aaron, David, etc., or of both parents , but more especially of their fathers , and fancied that owing to these they could not but be pleasing to God; but John declares that these very things have no weight [with Him]. ἀλλʼ ἐκ Θεοῦ , but of God ) To the natural generation of men is opposed generation of God. And although the former, as the latter, is in reality single, yet the former being expressed in a threefold manner [&ldquo;infert,&rdquo; causes] carries with it a threefold mode of viewing the latter. We are therefore taught, that they become Sons of God , who are born, n</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv13_2').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Robertson's Word Pictures</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1933)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv13_2" class="collapsed comm-body">Which were born ( ο εγεννηθησαν ). First aorist passive indicative of γενναω , to beget, "who were begotten." By spiritual generation (of God, εκ θεου ), not by physical ( εξ αιματων , plural as common in classics and O.T., though why it is not clear unless blood of both father and mother; εκ θεληματος σαρκος , from sexual desire; εκ θεληματος ανδρος , from the will of the male). But b of the old Latin reads qui natus est and makes it refer to Christ and so expressly teach the Virgin Birth of Jesus. Likewise Irenaeus reads qui natus est as does Tertullian who argues that qui nati sunt ( ο εγεννηθησαν ) is an invention of the Valentinian Gnostics. Blass (Philology of the Gospels, p. 234) opposes this reading, but all the old Greek uncials read ο εγεννηθησαν and it must be accepted. The Virgin Birth is doubtless implied in verse [John 1:14], but it is not stated in verse [John 1:13].</div></div><div class="themes-divider">🔍 Temas discutidos</div><div class="theme-card"><div class="theme-word">οἱ ἐγεννήθησαν</div><div class="consensus-bar"><div style="width:25%;background:#f44336"></div></div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#4caf50">✅ <strong>Alford</strong> Las conjunciones οὐδὲ... οὐδέ forman un clímax ascendente, no meramente disyuntivo</div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#4caf50">✅ <strong>Robertson</strong> Todos los manuscritos griegos unciales leen οἱ ἐγεννήθησαν (plural), no qui natus est (singular) del latín</div><div class="theme-summary">Hay debate textual sobre si el verbo es singular (refiriéndose a Cristo) o plural (refiriéndose a los creyentes), con los manuscritos griegos favoreciendo el plural.</div></div></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('patr-13')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="patr-13" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">👨‍🏫</span> Patrística · 3 temas · 22 citas <span class="arrow" id="arrow-patr-13">▶</span></div><div id="patr-13" class="collapsed section-content patr-section" role="region"><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt86f24c2c').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Nacimiento espiritual versus carnal</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt86f24c2c" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Agustín de Hipona</strong> (354-430) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.13]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"And how are they born? Because they become sons of God and brethren of Christ, they are certainly born. For if they are not born, how can they be sons? But the sons of men are born of flesh and blood, and of the will of man, and of the embrace of wedlock. But in what manner are they born? 'Who not of bloods,' as if of male and female. Bloods is not Latin; but because it is plural in Greek, the interpreter preferred so to express it, and to speak bad Latin according to the grammarian that he might speak true divinity according to God."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Juan Crisóstomo</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.13]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"'Who were born, not of blood, nor of the will of the flesh, but of God.' This he has done, in order that, considering the vileness, and lowness of the first birth, which is 'of blood,' and 'the will of the flesh,' and perceiving the highness and nobleness of the second, which is by grace, we may form from thence some great opinion of it, and one worthy of the gift of Him who hath begotten us, and for the future exhibit much earnestness."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Clemente de Alejandría</strong> (c.150-215) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.13]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"For not only must the idols which he formerly held as gods, but the works also of his former life, be abandoned by him who has been 'born again, not of blood, nor of the will of the flesh,' but in the Spirit; which consists in repenting by not giving way to the same fault."</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres contrastan claramente el nacimiento natural (de sangre y voluntad humana) con el nacimiento espiritual que viene de Dios. Este último es superior y requiere abandono de la vida anterior.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('pt77beae3a').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Controversia textual sobre singular vs plural</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:55%;background:#ff9800"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#ff9800">medio</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="pt77beae3a" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#f44336"><div class="patr-cite-header">❌ <strong>Tertuliano</strong> (c.160-225) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.13]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"What, then, is the meaning of this passage, 'Born not of blood, nor of the will of the flesh, nor of the will of man, but of God?' I shall make more use of this passage after I have confuted those who have tampered with it. They maintain that it was written thus (in the plural) 'Who were born, not of blood, nor of the will of the flesh, nor of the will of man, but of God,' as if designating those who were before mentioned as 'believing in His name,' in order to point out the existence"</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Ireneo</strong> (c.130-202) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.13]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Matthew might certainly have said, 'Now the birth of Jesus was on this wise;' but the Holy Ghost, foreseeing the corrupters [of the truth], and guarding by anticipation against their deceit, says by Matthew, 'But the birth of Christ was on this wise;' and that He is Emmanuel, lest perchance we might consider Him as a mere man: for 'not by the will of the flesh nor by the will of man, but by the will of God was the Word made flesh;'"</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Existe debate sobre si Juan 1:13 se refiere al nacimiento de Cristo (singular) o de los creyentes (plural). Tertuliano defiende la lectura singular mientras otros padres usan la plural.</div></div></div><div class="patr-theme"><div class="patr-theme-header" onclick="document.getElementById('ptda4dd0b3').classList.toggle('collapsed');this.querySelector('.arrow').classList.toggle('open')"><strong>Encarnación y divinización mutua</strong><div class="consensus-bar" style="width:60px"><div style="width:85%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span class="consensus-label" style="color:#4caf50">alto</span><span class="arrow">▼</span></div><div id="ptda4dd0b3" class="collapsed" style="padding:0.5rem 0.2rem 0"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Juan Crisóstomo</strong> (c.349-407) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.12]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"Having declared that they who received Him were 'born of God,' and had become 'sons of God,' he adds the cause and reason of this unspeakable honor. It is that 'the Word became Flesh,' that the Master took on Him the form of a servant. For He became Son of man, who was God's own Son, in order that He might make the sons of men to be children of God."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Ireneo</strong> (c.130-202) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.13]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"For it was for this end that the Word of God was made man, and He who was the Son of God became the Son of man, that man, having been taken into the Word, and receiving the adoption, might become the son of God. For by no other means could we have attained to incorruptibility and immortality, unless we had been united to incorruptibility and immortality."</div></div><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#4caf50"><div class="patr-cite-header">✅ <strong>Teodoreto de Ciro</strong> (c.393-458) <span class="patr-verse-ref">[v.12]</span></div><div class="patr-cite-text">"For this is why the Word became a human being and the Son of God became a Son of man: that the human being, by embracing the Word and receiving adoption, might become"</div></div><div class="patr-resumen">Los Padres enseñan el intercambio admirable: Cristo se hizo hombre para que los hombres pudieran hacerse hijos de Dios. La encarnación es el fundamento de la divinización humana.</div></div></div></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('tc-13')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="tc-13" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">⚖️</span> Crítica Textual <span style="font-size:0.7rem;color:#ff9800">(5 lecturas)</span> <span class="arrow" id="arrow-tc-13">▶</span></div><div id="tc-13" class="collapsed section-content tc-section"><div class="tc-verdict" style="margin-bottom:0.8rem"><div class="tc-verdict-text"><strong>Veredicto:</strong> La lectura #3.1 (οἳ οὐκ... ἐγεννήθησαν) en plural es probablemente original, con fuerte apoyo de P66, א, B, C y la mayoría de manuscritos. La lectura #3.4 (ὃς οὐκ... ἐγεννήθη) en singular representa una alteración teológica para referirse específicamente al nacimiento virginal de Cristo. Las lecturas #3.2 y #3.3 son variantes menores en la forma verbal, mientras que #3.5 omite la frase completamente.</div><div class="consensus-bar" style="max-width:200px"><div style="width:90%;background:#4caf50"></div></div><span style="font-size:0.72rem;color:#4caf50;font-weight:600;margin-left:4px">Confianza: alta</span><div class="tc-impact"><strong>Impacto:</strong> La diferencia entre plural y singular es teológicamente crucial: el plural se refiere al nacimiento espiritual de todos los creyentes, mientras que el singular se refiere específicamente al nacimiento virginal de Cristo. Esta variante refleja debates cristológicos tempranos sobre la naturaleza del nacimiento de Cristo.</div></div><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin-bottom:0.5rem"><table class="tc-table"><tr class="tc-header"><th class="tc-ms-col">MS</th><th class="tc-var-col" title="Columna variante 1: οἳ">⚡1</th><th class="tc-var-col" title="Columna variante 2: οὐκ">⚡2</th><th class="tc-ctx">ἐξ</th><th class="tc-ctx">αἱμάτων</th></tr><tr><td class="tc-ms-cell" onclick="showMSSPanel('… ἐγεννήθησαν (see also footnote 4) 𝔓66 א B2 C Dc L Wsupp Ψ 0141 f1 f13 33 180 205 565 579 597 700 892 1006 1010 1241 1243 1292 1342 1424 1505 Byz [E F G H] Lect itaur, c, e, f, ff2, q vg syrp, h, pal copsa, bo arm eth geo slav Valentiniansacc. to Tertullian Origengr, lat 1/2 Eusebius Asterius Athanasius Ps-Athanasius Marcellus Cyril-Jerusalem Didymusdub Macarius/Symeon Epiphanius Chrysostom Severian Cyril Theodotus-Ancyra Hesychius Theodoret; Ambrosiaster Hilary Ambrose3/5 Chr')"><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0" data-s="4" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'4');">4</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#b71c1c;color:white;font-weight:700" data-s="𝔓66" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'𝔓66');">𝔓66</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#1565c0;color:white;font-weight:700" data-s="א" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'א');">א</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#1565c0;color:white;font-weight:700" data-s="C" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'C');">C</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#1565c0;color:white;font-weight:700" data-s="L" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'L');">L</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#fff3e0;color:#e65100" data-s="Wsupp" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'Wsupp');">Wsupp</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#1565c0;color:white;font-weight:700" data-s="Ψ" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'Ψ');">Ψ</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#1976d2;color:white" data-s="0141" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'0141');">0141</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#f57f17;color:white" data-s="f1" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'f1');">f1</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#f57f17;color:white" data-s="f13" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'f13');">f13</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0" data-s="33" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'33');">33</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0" data-s="180" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'180');">180</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0" data-s="205" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'205');">205</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0" data-s="565" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'565');">565</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0" data-s="579" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'579');">579</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0" data-s="597" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'597');">597</span><span class="ms-chip" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0" data-s="700" onclick="event.stopPropagation();showMSInfo(this,'700');">700</span><span class="ms-ch