20">Τί οὖν Ἠλίας εἶ</span></span><span style="margin-right:0.8rem">#3: <span style="font-family:serif;color:#1b5e20">Τί οὖν; Ἠλίας εἶ σύ</span></span><span style="margin-right:0.8rem">#4: <span style="font-family:serif;color:#1b5e20">Σὺ οὖν τί; Ἠλίας εἶ</span></span><span style="margin-right:0.8rem">#5: <span style="font-family:serif;color:#1b5e20">Σὺ τίς εἶ; Ἠλίας εἶ</span></span></div><div style="font-size:0.63rem;color:#999;margin-top:2px;display:flex;gap:0.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><span style="font-weight:600">MSS:</span> <span>🔴 Papiros</span> <span>🔵 Unciales</span> <span>⚪ Minúsc.</span> <span>🟣 Versiones</span> <span>🟠 Padres</span> <span>🟢 Byz/Lect</span></div><div class="tc-criteria-expanded"><div class="tc-criterion-item"><strong>Apoyo mayoritario</strong><div class="tc-criterion-exp">La lectura #7.3 tiene el apoyo de la mayoría de manuscritos y diversas tradiciones textuales. Esta amplia atestación sugiere que preserva la forma original.</div></div><div class="tc-criterion-item"><strong>Estructura retórica</strong><div class="tc-criterion-exp">La forma 'Τί οὖν; Ἠλίας εἶ σύ' mantiene el patrón de preguntas directas en el contexto del interrogatorio. Las otras variantes parecen ser reordenamientos estilísticos.</div></div></div><div style="font-size:0.72rem;color:#1565c0;margin-top:0.5rem;cursor:pointer" onclick="document.getElementById('exeg-21')?.classList.remove('collapsed');document.getElementById('exeg-21')?.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'})">↑ Ver análisis exegético de este versículo</div><div style="margin-top:0.8rem;text-align:center"><a href="tc_deep_dive_John_1_21.html" onclick="if(!this.dataset.ready){this.textContent='⏳ Generando análisis profundo...';this.style.opacity=0.6;return true;}" style="display:inline-block;padding:8px 20px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a237e,#0d47a1);color:white;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.85rem;font-weight:600;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(26,35,126,0.3)">🔍 Deep Dive — Análisis completo de esta variante</a><div style="font-size:0.7rem;color:#888;margin-top:3px">Si la página no existe, usa el tool <code>critical_apparatus</code> → <code>tc_deep_dive</code> en el MCP server para generarla.</div></div></div></div><div class="verse-block" id="vb22"><div class="verse-header"><span class="vnum">22</span></div><div class="greek-line" id="greek-22">Εἶπαν οὖν αὐτῷ Τίς εἶ ἵνα ἀπόκρισιν δῶμεν τοῖς πέμψασιν ἡμᾶς τί λέγεις περὶ σεαυτοῦ</div><div class="uncial-line" id="uncial-22" style="display:none;font-family:'Noto Serif',serif;font-size:0.9rem;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#5d4037;background:#efebe9;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;overflow-wrap:break-word" title="Así se vería este versículo en un manuscrito uncial del siglo IV — todo mayúsculas, sin espacios (puntos medios añadidos como ayuda visual)">ΕΙΠΑΝ·ΟΥΝ·ΑΥΤΩΙ·ΤΙΣ·ΕΙ·ΙΝΑ·ΑΠΟΚΡΙΣΙΝ·ΔΩΜΕΝ·ΤΟΙΣ·ΠΕΜΨΑΣΙΝ·ΗΜΑΣ·ΤΙ·ΛΕΓΕΙΣ·ΠΕΡΙ·ΣΕΑΥΤΟΥ<span style="display:block;font-size:0.65rem;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:0;opacity:0.7"><a href="https://www.codexsinaiticus.org/en/manuscript.aspx?book=33&chapter=1&verse=22" target="_blank" style="color:#5d4037">Ver en Codex Sinaiticus →</a></span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:0.3rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:0.3rem;align-items:center"><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="toggleRVR(22)">RVR60</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('uncial-22').style.display=document.getElementById('uncial-22').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#efebe9;color:#5d4037;border-color:#bcaaa4" title="Escritura uncial: así se veía el NT en los manuscritos del s.IV (Vaticanus, Sinaiticus). Todo mayúsculas, sin espacios entre palabras (scriptio continua), sin acentos ni puntuación. La iota subscrita se escribe explícitamente.">Uncial</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('pron-22').style.display=document.getElementById('pron-22').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" style="background:#e3f2fd;color:#1565c0;border-color:#90caf9" title="Pronunciación bizantina aproximada (griego moderno/eclesiástico)">Pronunciación</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-patr" onclick="toggleSection('patr-22')" title="4 citas patrísticas disponibles">✝ 4 patrística</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-exeg" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-22')" title="3 comentarios exegéticos">📚 3 exégesis</div><div class="rvr-btn vbtn-ver" onclick="document.getElementById('vers-22').classList.toggle('collapsed')" title="9 versiones disponibles">📖 versiones</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="copyVerse(22)" title="Copiar versículo al portapapeles" style="background:#f3e5f5;border-color:#ce93d8;color:#6a1b9a">📋</div><div class="rvr-btn" onclick="document.getElementById('notes-22').style.display=document.getElementById('notes-22').style.display==='none'?'':'none'" title="Notas personales" style="background:#fff8e1;border-color:#ffd54f;color:#f57f17">📝</div></div><div id="rvr-22" class="collapsed spanish-line">Le dijeron: ¿Pues quién eres? para que demos respuesta a los que nos enviaron. ¿Qué dices de ti mismo?</div><div id="vers-22" class="collapsed" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem"><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR60</span>Le dijeron: ¿Pues quién eres? para que demos respuesta a los que nos enviaron. ¿Qué dices de ti mismo?</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">RVR1909</span>Dijéronle: ¿Pues quién eres? para que demos respuesta á los que nos enviaron. ¿Qué dices de ti mismo?</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">KJV</span>Then said they unto him, Who art thou? that we may give an answer to them that sent us. What sayest thou of thyself?</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">ASV</span>They said therefore unto him, Who art thou? that we may give an answer to them that sent us. What sayest thou of thyself? </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">BSB</span>So they said to him, “Who are you? We need an answer for those who sent us. What do you say about yourself?” </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Darby</span>They said therefore to him, Who art thou? that we may give an answer to those who sent us. What sayest thou of thyself? </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">LITV</span>Then they said to him, Who are you, that we may give an answer to those sending us? What do you say about yourself? </div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">YLT</span>They said then to him, `Who art thou, that we may give an answer to those sending us? what dost thou say concerning thyself?'</div><div class="ver-line"><span class="ver-label">Vulgate</span>dixerunt ergo ei quis es ut responsum demus his qui miserunt nos quid dicis de te ipso</div></div><div id="pron-22" style="display:none;font-size:0.85rem;color:#1565c0;background:#e3f2fd;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:0.3rem;font-style:italic" class="pron-line"></div><div id="notes-22" style="display:none;margin-bottom:0.5rem"><textarea id="note-input-22" style="width:100%;min-height:50px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;padding:4px 8px;font-size:0.82rem;resize:vertical" placeholder="Tus notas para v.22..." oninput="saveNote(22)"></textarea></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('exeg-22')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="exeg-22" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">📜</span> Exégesis del Griego <span class="arrow" id="arrow-exeg-22">▶</span></div><div id="exeg-22" class="collapsed section-content exeg-section" role="region"><div class="exeg-summary"><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Alford:</strong> ] Notice they ever ask about his person: he ever refers them to his office.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Bengel:</strong> περί , concerning ) Each man himself ought) to know himself [ and, if he has any undertaking in particular, he ought to have in readiness a reason [to give] of his undertaking.<br><strong style="color:#1b5e20">Robertson:</strong> They said therefore ( ειπαν ουν ).<br></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv22_0').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Alford's Greek Testament</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1863)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv22_0" class="collapsed comm-body">22. ] Notice they ever ask about his person: he ever refers them to his office . He is no one a voice merely: it is the work of God, the testimony to Christ which is every thing. So the formalist ever in the church asks Who is he? while the witness for Christ only exalts, only cares for Christ&rsquo;s work.</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv22_1').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Bengel's Gnomon</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1742)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv22_1" class="collapsed comm-body">[John 1:22] . Ἀπόκρισιν δῶμεν , may give an answer ) The people had demanded an answer, and especially the Jewish chief priests. περί , concerning ) Each man himself ought) to know himself [ and, if he has any undertaking in particular, he ought to have in readiness a reason [to give] of his undertaking . V. g.]</div></div><div class="comm-item"><div class="comm-header" onclick="document.getElementById('uexv22_2').classList.toggle('collapsed')"><strong>Robertson's Word Pictures</strong> <span style=color:#888;font-size:0.75rem>(1933)</span><span class="small-arrow">ver completo ▼</span></div><div id="uexv22_2" class="collapsed comm-body">They said therefore ( ειπαν ουν ). Second aorist active indicative of defective verb ειπον with α instead of usual ο . Note ουν , inferential here as in verse [John 1:21] though often merely transitional in John. Who art thou? ( Τις ει; ). Same question as at first (verse [John 1:19]), but briefer. That we give answer ( ινα αποκρισιν δωμεν ). Final use of ινα with second aorist active subjunctive of διδωμ with αποκρισιν from αποκρινομα , above, old substantive as in [Luke 2:47]. To those that sent ( τοις πεμψασιν ). Dative case plural of the articular participle first aorist active of πεμπω . What sayest thou of thyself? ( Τ λεγεις περ σεαυτου; ). This time they opened wide the door without giving any hint at all.</div></div><div class="themes-divider">🔍 Temas discutidos</div><div class="theme-card"><div class="theme-word">τίς εἶ / ἀπόκρισιν δῶμεν</div><div class="consensus-bar"><div style="width:55%;background:#ff9800"></div></div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#4caf50">✅ <strong>Alford</strong> Ellos preguntan sobre su persona, él siempre se refiere a su oficio - es solo una voz, no alguien importante</div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#ff9800">⚠️ <strong>Bengel</strong> Cada hombre debe conocerse a sí mismo y tener preparada una razón de su empresa</div><div class="opinion" style="border-left-color:#4caf50">✅ <strong>Robertson</strong> Esta vez abrieron completamente la puerta sin dar ninguna pista (τί λέγεις περὶ σεαυτοῦ)</div><div class="theme-summary">Alford y Robertson se enfocan en la dinámica de la pregunta, mientras Bengel añade una reflexión sobre el autoconocimiento.</div></div></div><div class="section-toggle" onclick="toggleSection('patr-22')" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="patr-22" tabindex="0"><span class="section-icon">👨‍🏫</span> Patrística (4 citas) <span class="arrow" id="arrow-patr-22">▶</span></div><div id="patr-22" class="collapsed section-content patr-section" role="region"><div class="patr-citation" style="border-left-color:#9e9e9e"><div class="patr-cite-header"><strong>Chrysostom - Homilies on Timothy-Hebrews</strong> <em>(Homily XVI.)</em></div><div class="patr-cite-text">2. Hear then how this blessed person answered to the intention with which they asked
