, [phrase] besiege, bring (forth, in, into, to pass), call, carry, [idiom] certainly, (cause, let", "s": "H935", "d": "to go or come (in a wide variety of applications)", "es": ""}], "13": [{"w": "בָּ֣ז", "l": "בּוּז", "m": "HVqrmsa", "g": "contemn, despise, [idiom] utterly.", "s": "H936", "d": "to disrespect", "es": ""}, {"w": "לְ֭/דָבָר", "l": "דָּבָר", "m": "HR/Ncmsa", "g": "act, advice, affair, answer, [idiom] any such (thing), because of, book, business, care, case, cause, certain rate, [phrase] chronicles, commandment", "s": "H1697", "d": "a word; by implication, a matter (as spoken of) or thing; adverbially, a cause", "es": ""}, {"w": "יֵחָ֣בֶל", "l": "חָבַל", "m": "HVNi3ms", "g": "[idiom] at all, band, bring forth, (deal) corrupt(-ly), destroy, offend, lay to (take a) pledge, spoil, travail, [idiom] very, withhold.", "s": "H2254", "d": "to wind tightly (as a rope), i.e. to bind; specifically, by a pledge; figuratively, to pervert, destroy; also to writhe in pain (especially of parturition)", "es": ""}, {"w": "ל֑/וֹ", "l": "", "m": "HR/Sp3ms", "g": "", "s": "", "d": "", "es": ""}, {"w": "וִ/ירֵ֥א", "l": "יָרֵא", "m": "HC/Aamsc", "g": "afraid, fear (-ful).", "s": "H3373", "d": "fearing; morally, reverent", "es": ""}, {"w": "מִ֝צְוָ֗ה", "l": "מִצְוָה", "m": "HNcfsa", "g": "(which was) commanded(-ment), law, ordinance, precept.", "s": "H4687", "d": "a command, whether human or divine (collectively, the Law)", "es": ""}, {"w": "ה֣וּא", "l": "הוּא", "m": "HPp3ms", "g": "he, as for her, him(-self), it, the same, she (herself), such, that (...it), these, they, this, those, which (is), who.", "s": "H1931", "d": "he (she or it); only expressed when emphatic or without a verb; also (intensively) self, or (especially with the article) the same; sometimes (as demonstrative) this or that; occasionally (instead of copula) as or are", "es": ""}, {"w": "יְשֻׁלָּֽם", "l": "שָׁלַם", "m": "HVPi3ms", "g": "make amends, (make an) end, finish, full, give again, make good, (re-) pay (again), (make) (to) (be at) peace(-able), that is perfect, perform", "s": "H7999", "d": "to be safe (in mind, body or estate); figuratively, to be (causatively, make) completed; by implication, to be friendly; by extension, to reciprocate (in various applications)", "es": ""}], "14": [{"w": "תּוֹרַ֣ת", "l": "תּוֹרָה", "m": "HNcfsc", "g": "law.", "s": "H8451", "d": "a precept or statute, especially the Decalogue or Pentateuch", "es": ""}, {"w": "חָ֭כָם", "l": "חָכָם", "m": "HAamsa", "g": "cunning (man), subtil, (un-), wise((hearted), man).", "s": "H2450", "d": "wise, (i.e. intelligent, skilful or artful)", "es": ""}, {"w": "מְק֣וֹר", "l": "מָקוֹר", "m": "HNcmsc", "g": "fountain, issue, spring, well(-spring).", "s": "H4726", "d": "properly, something dug, i.e. a (general) source (of water, even when naturally flowing; also of tears, blood (by euphemism, of the female pudenda); figuratively, of happiness, wisdom, progeny)", "es": ""}, {"w": "חַיִּ֑ים", "l": "חַי", "m": "HNcmpa", "g": "[phrase] age, alive, appetite, (wild) beast, company, congregation, life(-time), live(-ly), living (creature, thing), maintenance, [phrase] merry", "s": "H2416", "d": "alive; hence, raw (flesh); fresh (plant, water, year), strong; also (as noun, especially in the feminine singular and masculine plural) life (or living thing), whether literally or figuratively", "es": ""}, {"w": "לָ֝/ס֗וּר", "l": "סוּר", "m": "HR/Vqc", "g": "be(-head), bring, call back, decline, depart, eschew, get (you), go (aside), [idiom] grievous, lay away (by), leave undone, be past, pluck away", "s": "H5493", "d": "to turn off (literal or figurative)", "es": ""}, {"w": "מִ/מֹּ֥קְשֵׁי", "l": "מוֹקֵשׁ", "m": "HR/Ncmpc", "g": "be ensnared, gin, (is) snare(-d), trap.", "s": "H4170", "d": "a noose (for catching animals) (literally or figuratively); by implication, a hook (for the nose)", "es": ""}, {"w": "מָֽוֶת", "l": "מָוֶת", "m": "HNcmsa", "g": "(be) dead(-ly), death, die(-d).", "s": "H4194", "d": "death (natural or violent); concretely, the dead, their place or state (hades); figuratively, pestilence, ruin", "es": ""}], "15": [{"w": "שֵֽׂכֶל", "l": "שֶׂכֶל", "m": "HNcmsa", "g": "discretion, knowledge, policy, prudence, sense, understanding, wisdom, wise.", "s": "H7922", "d": "intelligence; by implication, success", "es": ""}, {"w": "ט֭וֹב", "l": "טוֹב", "m": "HAamsa", "g": "beautiful, best, better, bountiful, cheerful, at ease, [idiom] fair (word), (be in) favour, fine, glad, good (deed, -lier, -liest, -ly, -ness, -s)", "s": "H2896", "d": "good (as an adjective) in the widest sense; used likewise as a noun, both in the masculine and the feminine, the singular and the plural (good, a good or good thing, a good man or woman; the good, goods or good things, good men or women), also as an adverb (well)", "es": ""}, {"w": "יִתֶּן", "l": "נָתַן", "m": "HVqi3ms", "g": "add, apply, appoint, ascribe, assign, [idiom] avenge, [idiom] be (healed), bestow, bring (forth, hither), cast, cause, charge, come, commit, consider", "s": "H5414", "d": "to give, used with greatest latitude of application (put, make, etc.)", "es": ""}, {"w": "חֵ֑ן", "l": "חֵן", "m": "HNcmsa", "g": "favour, grace(-ious), pleasant, precious, (well-) favoured.", "s": "H2580", "d": "graciousness, i.e. subjective (kindness, favor) or objective (beauty)", "es": ""}, {"w": "וְ/דֶ֖רֶךְ", "l": "דֶּרֶךְ", "m": "HC/Ncbsc", "g": "along, away, because of, [phrase] by, conversation, custom, (east-) ward, journey, manner, passenger, through, toward, (high-) (path-) way(-side)", "s": "H1870", "d": "a road (as trodden); figuratively, a course of life or mode of action, often adverb", "es": ""}, {"w": "בֹּגְדִ֣ים", "l": "בָּגַד", "m": "HVqrmpa", "g": "deal deceitfully (treacherously, unfaithfully), offend, transgress(-or), (depart), treacherous (dealer, -ly, man), unfaithful(-ly, man), [idiom] very.", "s": "H898", "d": "to cover (with a garment); figuratively, to act covertly; by implication, to pillage", "es": ""}, {"w": "אֵיתָֽן", "l": "אֵיתָן", "m": "HAamsa", "g": "hard, mighty, rough, strength, strong.", "s": "H386", "d": "permanence; hence (concrete) permanent; specifically a chieftain", "es": ""}], "16": [{"w": "כָּל", "l": "כֹּל", "m": "HNcmsc", "g": "(in) all (manner, (ye)), altogether, any (manner), enough, every (one, place, thing), howsoever, as many as, (no-) thing, ought, whatsoever", "s": "H3605", "d": "properly, the whole; hence, all, any or every (in the singular only, but often in a plural sense)", "es": ""}, {"w": "עָ֭רוּם", "l": "עָרוּם", "m": "HAamsa", "g": "crafty, prudent, subtil.", "s": "H6175", "d": "cunning (usually in a bad sense)", "es": ""}, {"w": "יַעֲשֶׂ֣ה", "l": "עָשָׂה", "m": "HVqi3ms", "g": "accomplish, advance, appoint, apt, be at, become, bear, bestow, bring forth, bruise, be busy, [idiom] certainly, have the charge of, commit", "s": "H6213", "d": "to do or make, in the broadest sense and widest application", "es": ""}, {"w": "בְ/דָ֑עַת", "l": "דַּעַת", "m": "HR/Ncfsa", "g": "cunning, (ig-) norantly, know(-ledge), (un-) awares (wittingly).", "s": "H1847", "d": "knowledge", "es": ""}, {"w": "וּ֝/כְסִ֗יל", "l": "כְּסִיל", "m": "HC/Aamsa", "g": "fool(-ish).", "s": "H3684", "d": "properly, fat, i.e. (figuratively) stupid or silly", "es": ""}, {"w": "יִפְרֹ֥שׂ", "l": "פָּרַשׂ", "m": "HVqi3ms", "g": "break, chop in pieces, lay open, scatter, spread (abroad, forth, selves, out), stretch (forth, out).", "s": "H6566", "d": "to break apart, disperse, etc.", "es": ""}, {"w": "אִוֶּֽלֶת", "l": "אִוֶּלֶת", "m": "HNcfsa", "g": "folly, foolishly(-ness).", "s": "H200", "d": "silliness", "es": ""}], "17": [{"w": "מַלְאָ֣ךְ", "l": "מֲלְאָךְ", "m": "HNcmsa", "g": "ambassador, angel, king, messenger.", "s": "H4397", "d": "a messenger; specifically, of God, i.e. an angel (also a prophet, priest or teacher)", "es": ""}, {"w": "רָ֭שָׁע", "l": "רָשָׁע", "m": "HAamsa", "g": "[phrase] condemned, guilty, ungodly, wicked (man), that did wrong.", "s": "H7563", "d": "morally wrong; concretely, an (actively) bad person", "es": ""}, {"w": "יִפֹּ֣ל", "l": "נָפַל", "m": "HVqi3ms", "g": "be accepted, cast (down, self, (lots), out), cease, die, divide (by lot), (let) fail, (cause to, let, make, ready to) fall (away, down, -en, -ing)", "s": "H5307", "d": "to fall, in a great variety of applications (intransitive or causative, literal or figurative)", "es": ""}, {"w": "בְּ/רָ֑ע", "l": "רַע", "m": "HR/Aamsa", "g": "adversity, affliction, bad, calamity, [phrase] displease(-ure), distress, evil((-favouredness), man, thing), [phrase] exceedingly, [idiom] great", "s": "H7451", "d": "bad or (as noun) evil (natural or moral)", "es": ""}, {"w": "וְ/צִ֖יר", "l": "צִיר", "m": "HC/Ncmsc", "g": "ambassador, hinge, messenger, pain, pang, sorrow. Compare H6736 (צִיר).", "s": "H6735", "d": "a hinge (as pressed in turning); also a throe (as a phys. or mental pressure); also a herald or erranddoer (as constrained by the principal)", "es": ""}, {"w": "אֱמוּנִ֣ים", "l": "אֵמוּן", "m": "HNcmpa", "g": "faith(-ful), truth.", "s": "H529", "d": "established, i.e. (figuratively) trusty; also (abstractly) trustworthiness", "es": ""}, {"w": "מַרְפֵּֽא", "l": "מַרְפֵּא", "m": "HNcmsa", "g": "(in-)cure(-able), healing(-lth), remedy, sound, wholesome, yielding.", "s": "H4832", "d": "properly, curative, i.e. literally (concretely) a medicine, or (abstractly) a cure; figuratively (concretely) deliverance, or (abstractly) placidity", "es": ""}], "18": [{"w": "רֵ֣ישׁ", "l": "רֵישׁ", "m": "HNcmsa", "g": "poverty.", "s": "H7389", "d": "poverty", "es": ""}, {"w": "וְ֭/קָלוֹן", "l": "קָלוֹן", "m": "HC/Ncmsa", "g": "confusion, dishonour, ignominy, reproach, shame.", "s": "H7036", "d": "disgrace; (by implication) the pudenda", "es": ""}, {"w": "פּוֹרֵ֣עַ", "l": "פָּרַע", "m": "HVqrmsa", "g": "avenge, avoid, bare, go back, let, (make) naked, set at nought, perish, refuse, uncover.", "s": "H6544", "d": "to loosen; by implication, to expose, dismiss; figuratively, absolve, begin", "es": ""}, {"w": "מוּסָ֑ר", "l": "מוּסָר", "m": "HNcmsa", "g": "bond, chastening(-eth), chastisement, check, correction, discipline, doctrine, instruction, rebuke.", "s": "H4148", "d": "properly, chastisement; figuratively, reproof, warning or instruction; also restraint", "es": ""}, {"w": "וְ/שׁוֹמֵ֖ר", "l": "שָׁמַר", "m": "HC/Vqrmsa", "g": "beward, be circumspect, take heed (to self), keep(-er, self), mark, look narrowly, observe, preserve, regard, reserve, save (self), sure", "s": "H8104", "d": "properly, to hedge about (as with thorns), i.e. guard; generally, to protect, attend to, etc.", "es": ""}, {"w": "תּוֹכַ֣חַת", "l": "תּוֹכֵחָה", "m": "HNcfsa", "g": "argument, [idiom] chastened, correction, reasoning, rebuke, reproof, [idiom] be (often) reproved.", "s": "H8433", "d": "chastisement; figuratively (by words) correction, refutation, proof (even in defence)", "es": ""}, {"w": "יְכֻבָּֽד", "l": "כָּבַד", "m": "HVPi3ms", "g": "abounding with, more grievously afflict, boast, be chargeable, [idiom] be dim, glorify, be (make) glorious (things), glory, (very) great, be grievous", "s": "H3513", "d": "to be heavy, i.e. in a bad sense (burdensome, severe, dull) or in a good sense (numerous, rich, honorable; causatively, to make weighty (in the same two senses)", "es": ""}], "19": [{"w": "תַּאֲוָ֣ה", "l": "תַּאֲוָה", "m": "HNcfsa", "g": "dainty, desire, [idiom] exceedingly, [idiom] greedily, lust(ing), pleasant. See also H6914 (קִבְרוֹת הַתַּאֲוָה).", "s": "H8378", "d": "a longing; by implication, a delight (subjectively, satisfaction, objectively, a charm)", "es": ""}, {"w": "נִ֭הְיָה", "l": "הָיָה", "m": "HVNrfsa", "g": "beacon, [idiom] altogether, be(-come), accomplished, committed, like), break, cause, come (to pass), do, faint, fall, [phrase] follow, happen", "s": "H1961", "d": "to exist, i.e. be or become, come to pass (always emphatic, and not a mere copula or auxiliary)", "es": ""}, {"w": "תֶּעֱרַ֣ב", "l": "עָרֵב", "m": "HVqi3fs", "g": "be pleasant(-ing), take pleasure in, be swee